---AgentCard conveys key information: - Overall details (version, name, description, uses) - Skills; a set of actions/solutions the agent can perform - Default modalities/content types supported by the agent. - Authentication requirements Next ID: 19
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.A2aV1AgentCard
---@field provider? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.A2aV1AgentProvider The service provider of the agent.
---@field version? string The version of the agent. Example: "1.0.0"
---@field description? string A description of the agent's domain of action/solution space. Example: "Agent that helps users with recipes and cooking."
---@field iconUrl? string An optional URL to an icon for the agent.
---@field additionalInterfaces? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.A2aV1AgentInterfaceList Announcement of additional supported transports. Client can use any of the supported transports.
---@field preferredTransport? string The transport of the preferred endpoint. If empty, defaults to JSONRPC.
---@field protocolVersion? string The version of the A2A protocol this agent supports.
---@field documentationUrl? string A url to provide additional documentation about the agent.
---@field defaultOutputModes? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList The mime types supported as outputs from this agent.
---@field defaultInputModes? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList protolint:enable REPEATED_FIELD_NAMES_PLURALIZED The set of interaction modes that the agent supports across all skills. This can be overridden per skill. Defined as mime types.
---@field security? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.A2aV1SecurityList protolint:disable REPEATED_FIELD_NAMES_PLURALIZED Security requirements for contacting the agent. This list can be seen as an OR of ANDs. Each object in the list describes one possible set of security requirements that must be present on a request. This allows specifying, for example, "callers must either use OAuth OR an API Key AND mTLS." Example: security { schemes { key: "oauth" value { list: ["read"] } } } security { schemes { key: "api-key" } schemes { key: "mtls" } }
---@field supportsAuthenticatedExtendedCard? boolean Whether the agent supports providing an extended agent card when the user is authenticated, i.e. is the card from .well-known different than the card from GetAgentCard.
