---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresSiteSearchEngineTargetSitesRequest
---@field siteVerificationInfo? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SiteVerificationInfo Output only. Site ownership and validity verification status.
---@field exactMatch? boolean Immutable. If set to false, a uri_pattern is generated to include all pages whose address contains the provided_uri_pattern. If set to true, an uri_pattern is generated to try to be an exact match of the provided_uri_pattern or just the specific page if the provided_uri_pattern is a specific one. provided_uri_pattern is always normalized to generate the URI pattern to be used by the search engine.
---@field rootDomainUri? string Output only. Root domain of the provided_uri_pattern.
---@field failureReason? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1TargetSiteFailureReason Output only. Failure reason.
---@field generatedUriPattern? string Output only. This is system-generated based on the provided_uri_pattern.
---@field type? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1TargetSiteTypeEnum|string The type of the target site, e.g., whether the site is to be included or excluded.
---@field providedUriPattern? string Required. Input only. The user provided URI pattern from which the `generated_uri_pattern` is generated.
---@field name? string Output only. The fully qualified resource name of the target site. `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/siteSearchEngine/targetSites/{target_site}` The `target_site_id` is system-generated.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The target site's last updated time.
---@field indexingStatus? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1TargetSiteIndexingStatusEnum|string Output only. Indexing status.
---@field parent string Required. Parent resource name of TargetSite, such as `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/siteSearchEngine`.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesAssistantsAgentsA2aV1TasksPushNotificationConfigsRequest
---@field name? string The resource name of the config. Format: tasks/{task_id}/pushNotificationConfigs/{config_id}
---@field pushNotificationConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.A2aV1PushNotificationConfig The push notification configuration details.
---@field tenant string Optional tenant, provided as a path parameter. Experimental, might still change for 1.0 release.
---@field parent string Required. The parent task resource for this config. Format: tasks/{task_id}
---@field configId? string Required. The ID for the new config.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesAssistantsRequest
---@field customerPolicy? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicy Optional. Customer policy for the assistant.
---@field displayName? string Required. The assistant display name. It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters.
---@field enabledTools? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantToolListMap Optional. The enabled tools on this assistant. The keys are data connector resource names, in the format `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataConnector`. The values are the tools that the admin enabled on that connector. Admins can selectively enable tools on any of the connectors that they created in the project. For example: ``` { "projects/my-project/locations/global/collections/jira1/dataConnector": { "toolInfo": [ { "toolName": "create_jira_issue", "toolDisplayName": "Create Jira issue" }, { "toolName": "update_jira_issue", "toolDisplayName": "Update Jira issue" } ] } } ```
---@field webGroundingType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantWebGroundingTypeEnum|string Optional. The type of web grounding to use.
---@field defaultWebGroundingToggleOff? boolean Optional. This field controls the default web grounding toggle for end users if `web_grounding_type` is set to `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_GOOGLE_SEARCH` or `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_ENTERPRISE_WEB_SEARCH`. By default, this field is set to false. If `web_grounding_type` is `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_GOOGLE_SEARCH` or `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_ENTERPRISE_WEB_SEARCH`, end users will have web grounding enabled by default on UI. If true, grounding toggle will be disabled by default on UI. End users can still enable web grounding in the UI if web grounding is enabled.
---@field description? string Optional. Description for additional information. Expected to be shown on the configuration UI, not to the users of the assistant.
---@field name? string Immutable. Resource name of the assistant. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/assistants/{assistant}` It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field generationConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantGenerationConfig Optional. Configuration for the generation of the assistant response.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Represents the time when this Assistant was most recently updated.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Represents the time when this Assistant was created.
---@field assistantId? string Required. The ID to use for the Assistant, which will become the final component of the Assistant's resource name. This field must conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) with a length limit of 63 characters.
---@field parent string Required. The parent resource name. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}`

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesControlsRequest
---@field redirectAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlRedirectAction Defines a redirect-type control.
---@field associatedServingConfigIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Output only. List of all ServingConfig IDs this control is attached to. May take up to 10 minutes to update after changes.
---@field conditions? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionList Determines when the associated action will trigger. Omit to always apply the action. Currently only a single condition may be specified. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field useCases? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlUseCasesItemEnumList Specifies the use case for the control. Affects what condition fields can be set. Only applies to SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH. Currently only allow one use case per control. Must be set when solution_type is SolutionType.SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. What solution the control belongs to. Must be compatible with vertical of resource. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field name? string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/*/locations/global/dataStore/*/controls/*`
---@field displayName? string Required. Human readable name. The identifier used in UI views. Must be UTF-8 encoded string. Length limit is 128 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field boostAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostAction Defines a boost-type control
---@field synonymsAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlSynonymsAction Treats a group of terms as synonyms of one another.
---@field filterAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlFilterAction Defines a filter-type control Currently not supported by Recommendation
---@field promoteAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlPromoteAction Promote certain links based on predefined trigger queries.
---@field controlId? string Required. The ID to use for the Control, which will become the final component of the Control's resource name. This value must be within 1-63 characters. Valid characters are /a-z-_/.
---@field parent string Required. Full resource name of parent data store. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}` or `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/engines/{engine_id}`.

