---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesRequest
---@field cmekConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CmekConfig Output only. CMEK-related information for the Engine.
---@field chatEngineMetadata? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineChatEngineMetadata Output only. Additional information of the Chat Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineIndustryVerticalEnum|string Optional. The industry vertical that the engine registers. The restriction of the Engine industry vertical is based on DataStore: Vertical on Engine has to match vertical of the DataStore linked to the engine.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Recommendation Engine was last updated.
---@field searchEngineConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfig Configurations for the Search Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Recommendation Engine was created at.
---@field sessionConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SessionConfig Optional. Non-empty default. Session config for the engine.
---@field connectorTenantInfo? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringMap Optional. Maps a connector ID (e.g., "hybrid-github", "shopify") to tenant-specific information required for that connector. The structure of the tenant information string is connector-dependent.
---@field modelConfigs? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineModelConfigsValueEnumMap Optional. Maps a model name to its specific configuration for this engine. This allows admin users to turn on/off individual models. This only stores models whose states are overridden by the admin. When the state is unspecified, or model_configs is empty for this model, the system will decide if this model should be available or not based on the default configuration. For example, a preview model should be disabled by default if the admin has not chosen to enable it.
---@field effectiveFeatures? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineEffectiveFeaturesValueEnumMap Output only. The complete, server-resolved state of every known feature toggle. Unlike `features`, which stores only explicit admin overrides, this map always contains an entry for every toggle. Clients should read toggle state from this field.
---@field associatedAgentRegistry? string Output only. The Agent registry containing the agents, MCP servers and tools associated with this engine. Derived server-side from the linked Agent Gateway's registry.
---@field observabilityConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ObservabilityConfig Optional. Observability config for the engine.
---@field chatEngineConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineChatEngineConfig Configurations for the Chat Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT.
---@field features? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturesValueEnumMap Optional. Feature config for the engine to opt in or opt out of features. Supported keys: * `*`: all features, if it's present, all other feature state settings are ignored. * `agent-gallery` * `no-code-agent-builder` * `prompt-gallery` * `model-selector` * `notebook-lm` * `people-search` * `people-search-org-chart` * `bi-directional-audio` * `speech-to-text` * `feedback` * `session-sharing` * `personalization-memory` * `personalization-suggested-highlights` * `mobile-app-access` * `disable-agent-sharing` * `disable-image-generation` * `disable-video-generation` * `music-generation` * `speech-generation` * `disable-onedrive-upload` * `disable-talk-to-content` * `disable-google-drive-upload` * `disable-welcome-emails` * `disable-canvas` * `canvas-workspace` * `canvas-app-builder` * `skills` * `skill-sharing` * `skill-sharing-without-admin-approval` * `skill-security-scan` * `disable-projects` * `sobi` * `enable-end-user-sharing-with-groups` * `single-agent-orchestration` * `multi-agent-orchestration` * `cross-product-intelligence` * `workflow-agents` * `in-app-notifications` * `code-extraction` * `remote-vm` * `license-tier-badge` * `canvas-app-sharing` * `agent-marketplace` * `agent-scheduling` * `preview-agents` * `plugins`
---@field globalFeatureToggleState? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineGlobalFeatureToggleStateEnum|string Optional. Controls the global feature toggle state for the engine.
---@field delayedGlobalFeatureToggleStateAllowed? boolean Output only. Whether the project is allowed to set `global_feature_toggle_state` to `DELAYED`.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the engine. Should be human readable. UTF-8 encoded string with limit of 1024 characters.
---@field procurementContactEmails? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. The emails of the procurement contacts.
---@field dataStoreIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. The data stores associated with this engine. For SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH and SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION type of engines, they can only associate with at most one data store. If solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT, multiple DataStores in the same Collection can be associated here. Note that when used in CreateEngineRequest, one DataStore id must be provided as the system will use it for necessary initializations.
---@field marketplaceAgentVisibility? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMarketplaceAgentVisibilityEnum|string Optional. The visibility of marketplace agents in the agent gallery.
---@field featurePolicies? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMap Optional. Per-feature access policies, keyed by feature toggle name (see `features`). A feature with no entry is available to every user when it is on. Only features that support access policies are accepted.
---@field mediaRecommendationEngineConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfig Configurations for the Media Engine. Only applicable on the data stores with solution_type SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION and IndustryVertical.MEDIA vertical.
---@field knowledgeGraphConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineKnowledgeGraphConfig Optional. Configurations for the Knowledge Graph. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field agentGatewaySetting? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AgentGatewaySetting Optional. The agent gateway setting for the engine.
---@field name? string Immutable. Identifier. The fully qualified resource name of the engine. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}` engine should be 1-63 characters, and valid characters are /a-z0-9*/. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field commonConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineCommonConfig Common config spec that specifies the metadata of the engine.
---@field disableAnalytics? boolean Optional. Whether to disable analytics for searches performed on this engine.
---@field appType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineAppTypeEnum|string Optional. Immutable. This the application type which this engine resource represents. NOTE: this is a new concept independ of existing industry vertical or solution type.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. The solutions of the engine.
---@field configurableBillingApproach? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineConfigurableBillingApproachEnum|string Optional. Configuration for configurable billing approach.
---@field parent string Required. The parent resource name, such as `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}`.
---@field engineId? string Required. The ID to use for the Engine, which will become the final component of the Engine's resource name. This field must conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) standard with a length limit of 63 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesServingConfigsRequest
---@field name? string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/engines/{engine_id}/servingConfigs/{serving_config_id}`
---@field synonymsControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition synonyms specifications. If multiple synonyms conditions match, all matching synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field diversityLevel? string How much diversity to use in recommendation model results e.g. `medium-diversity` or `high-diversity`. Currently supported values: * `no-diversity` * `low-diversity` * `medium-diversity` * `high-diversity` * `auto-diversity` If not specified, we choose default based on recommendation model type. Default value: `no-diversity`. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field promoteControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition promote specifications. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable serving config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field createTime? string Output only. ServingConfig created timestamp.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. ServingConfig updated timestamp.
---@field boostControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Boost controls to use in serving path. All triggered boost controls will be applied. Boost controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 boost controls.
---@field rankingExpression? string The ranking expression controls the customized ranking on retrieval documents. To leverage this, document embedding is required. The ranking expression setting in ServingConfig applies to all search requests served by the serving config. However, if `SearchRequest.ranking_expression` is specified, it overrides the ServingConfig ranking expression. The ranking expression is a single function or multiple functions that are joined by "+". * ranking_expression = function, { " + ", function }; Supported functions: * double * relevance_score * double * dotProduct(embedding_field_path) Function variables: * `relevance_score`: pre-defined keywords, used for measure relevance between query and document. * `embedding_field_path`: the document embedding field used with query embedding vector. * `dotProduct`: embedding function between embedding_field_path and query embedding vector. Example ranking expression: If document has an embedding field doc_embedding, the ranking expression could be `0.5 * relevance_score + 0.3 * dotProduct(doc_embedding)`.
---@field dissociateControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition do not associate specifications. If multiple do not associate conditions match, all matching do not associate controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field redirectControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList IDs of the redirect controls. Only the first triggered redirect action is applied, even if multiple apply. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field replacementControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition replacement specifications. Applied according to the order in the list. A previously replaced term can not be re-replaced. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field mediaConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ServingConfigMediaConfig The MediaConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field filterControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Filter controls to use in serving path. All triggered filter controls will be applied. Filter controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 filter controls.
---@field modelId? string The id of the model to use at serving time. Currently only RecommendationModels are supported. Can be changed but only to a compatible model (e.g. others-you-may-like CTR to others-you-may-like CVR). Required when SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field onewaySynonymsControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition oneway synonyms specifications. If multiple oneway synonyms conditions match, all matching oneway synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field ignoreControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition ignore specifications. If multiple ignore conditions match, all matching ignore controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field answerGenerationSpec? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AnswerGenerationSpec Optional. The specification for answer generation.
---@field genericConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ServingConfigGenericConfig The GenericConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ServingConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that a serving config can be associated with.
---@field parent string Required. Full resource name of parent. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}`
---@field servingConfigId? string Required. The ID to use for the ServingConfig, which will become the final component of the ServingConfig's resource name. This value should be 4-63 characters, and valid characters are /a-zA-Z0-9+/.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.CreateProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesSessionsRequest
---@field turns? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SessionTurnList Turns.
---@field labels? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. The labels for the session. Can be set as filter in ListSessionsRequest.
---@field pendingAsyncAssistOperationId? string Output only. Full resource name of an in-progress AsyncAssist operation for this session, e.g. `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/engines/*/sessions/*/operations/*`. Set when the operation starts and cleared when it finishes.
---@field isPinned? boolean Optional. Whether the session is pinned, pinned session will be displayed on the top of the session list.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the session finished.
---@field name? string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/sessions/*`
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of the session. This field is used to identify the session in the UI. By default, the display name is the first turn query text in the session.
