---AssistAnswer resource, main part of AssistResponse.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswer
---@field customerPolicyEnforcementResult? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResult Optional. The field contains information about the various policy checks' results like the banned phrases or the Model Armor checks. This field is populated only if the assist call was skipped due to a policy violation.
---@field state? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerStateEnum|string State of the answer generation.
---@field name? string Immutable. Identifier. Resource name of the `AssistAnswer`. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/sessions/{session}/assistAnswers/{assist_answer}` This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field replies? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerReplyList Replies of the assistant.
---@field toolDisplayNames? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringMap Output only. Maps a tool name (for example, `Internal-KB-Search` or `custom_mcp__agent__Internal-KB-Search`) to its human-readable display title (for example, `@Internal-KB Search`), populated from MCP tool `title` or `annotations.title` metadata so user-facing surfaces can display the tool title instead of the raw function declaration identifier. Empty when no tool display titles are present.
---@field assistSkippedReasons? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerAssistSkippedReasonsItemEnumList Reasons for not answering the assist call.
---@field connectorDisplayNames? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringMap Output only. Maps an internal connector agent name (the machine identifier embedded in tool names, e.g. `custom_mcp__agent`) to the connector's human-readable display name. Populated at serving time for custom MCP / agent gateway connectors so user-facing surfaces (e.g. the tool-call chip) can show the connector name instead of its internal identifier. Empty when there are no such connectors.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerAssistSkippedReasonsItemEnum "ASSIST_SKIPPED_REASON_UNSPECIFIED"|"NON_ASSIST_SEEKING_QUERY_IGNORED"|"CUSTOMER_POLICY_VIOLATION"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerAssistSkippedReasonsItemEnumList (gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerAssistSkippedReasonsItemEnum|string)[]

---Customer policy enforcement results. Contains the results of the various policy checks, like the banned phrases or the Model Armor checks.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResult
---@field violationSource? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultViolationSourceEnum|string Output only. The source of the violation.
---@field policyResults? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultPolicyEnforcementResultList Customer policy enforcement results. Populated only if the assist call was skipped due to a policy violation. It contains results from those filters that blocked the processing of the query.
---@field verdict? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultVerdictEnum|string Final verdict of the customer policy enforcement. If at least one policy blocked the processing, the verdict is BLOCK. If no policy blocked the processing but at least one flagged it, the verdict is FLAG.

---Customer policy enforcement result for the banned phrase policy.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultBannedPhraseEnforcementResult
---@field bannedPhrases? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList The banned phrases that were found in the query or the answer.

---Customer policy enforcement result for the Model Armor policy.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultModelArmorEnforcementResult
---@field modelArmorViolation? string The Model Armor violation that was found.
---@field error? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleRpcStatus The error returned by Model Armor if the policy enforcement failed for some reason.

---Customer policy enforcement result for a single policy type.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultPolicyEnforcementResult
---@field modelArmorEnforcementResult? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultModelArmorEnforcementResult The policy enforcement result for the Model Armor policy.
---@field bannedPhraseEnforcementResult? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultBannedPhraseEnforcementResult The policy enforcement result for the banned phrase policy.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultPolicyEnforcementResultList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultPolicyEnforcementResult[]

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultVerdictEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"ALLOW"|"BLOCK"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerCustomerPolicyEnforcementResultViolationSourceEnum "VIOLATION_SOURCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SYSTEM"|"PROMPT"|"ATTACHMENT"

---One part of the multi-part response of the assist call.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerReply
---@field groundedContent? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantGroundedContent Possibly grounded response text or media from the assistant.
---@field createTime? string The time when the reply was created.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerReplyList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistAnswerReply[]

