---@field fileId? string Required. The file ID.

---Customer-defined policy for the assistant.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicy
---@field bannedPhrases? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseList Optional. List of banned phrases.
---@field dataProtectionPolicy? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataProtectionPolicy Optional. Data protection policy to be used for sanitizing file uploads.
---@field modelArmorConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfig Optional. Model Armor configuration to be used for sanitizing user prompts and assistant responses.

---Definition of a customer-defined banned phrase. A banned phrase is not allowed to appear in the user query or the LLM response, or else the answer will be refused.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhrase
---@field ignoreDiacritics? boolean Optional. If true, diacritical marks (e.g., accents, umlauts) are ignored when matching banned phrases. For example, "cafe" would match "café".
---@field phrase? string Required. The raw string content to be banned.
---@field matchType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseMatchTypeEnum|string Optional. Match type for the banned phrase.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhrase[]

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseMatchTypeEnum "BANNED_PHRASE_MATCH_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SIMPLE_STRING_MATCH"|"WORD_BOUNDARY_STRING_MATCH"

---Configuration for customer defined Model Armor templates to be used for sanitizing user prompts and assistant responses.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfig
---@field userPromptTemplate? string Optional. The resource name of the Model Armor template for sanitizing user prompts. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/templates/{template_id}` If not specified, no sanitization will be applied to the user prompt.
---@field failureMode? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfigFailureModeEnum|string Optional. Defines the failure mode for Model Armor sanitization.
---@field responseTemplate? string Optional. The resource name of the Model Armor template for sanitizing assistant responses. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/templates/{template_id}` If not specified, no sanitization will be applied to the assistant response.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfigFailureModeEnum "FAILURE_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"FAIL_OPEN"|"FAIL_CLOSED"

---Configuration for the generation of the assistant response.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantGenerationConfig
---@field defaultModelId? string Optional. The default model to use for assistant.
---@field systemInstruction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantGenerationConfigSystemInstruction System instruction, also known as the prompt preamble for LLM calls. See also https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/learn/prompts/system-instructions
---@field allowedModelIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. The list of models that are allowed to be used for assistant.
---@field defaultLanguage? string The default language to use for the generation of the assistant response. Use an ISO 639-1 language code such as `en`. If not specified, the language will be automatically detected.

---System instruction, also known as the prompt preamble for LLM calls.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantGenerationConfigSystemInstruction
---@field additionalSystemInstruction? string Optional. Additional system instruction that will be added to the default system instruction.

---A piece of content and possibly its grounding information. Not all content needs grounding. Phrases like "Of course, I will gladly search it for you." do not need grounding.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantGroundedContent
---@field citationMetadata? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CitationMetadata Source attribution of the generated content. See also https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/learn/overview#citation_check
---@field textGroundingMetadata? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantGroundedContentTextGroundingMetadata Metadata for grounding based on text sources.
---@field content? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantContent The content.

