---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BatchVerifyTargetSitesRequest

---BigQuery source import data from.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigQuerySource
---@field gcsStagingDir? string Intermediate Cloud Storage directory used for the import with a length limit of 2,000 characters. Can be specified if one wants to have the BigQuery export to a specific Cloud Storage directory.
---@field tableId? string Required. The BigQuery table to copy the data from with a length limit of 1,024 characters.
---@field datasetId? string Required. The BigQuery data set to copy the data from with a length limit of 1,024 characters.
---@field dataSchema? string The schema to use when parsing the data from the source. Supported values for user event imports: * `user_event` (default): One UserEvent per row. Supported values for document imports: * `document` (default): One Document format per row. Each document must have a valid Document.id and one of Document.json_data or Document.struct_data. * `custom`: One custom data per row in arbitrary format that conforms to the defined Schema of the data store. This can only be used by the GENERIC Data Store vertical.
---@field partitionDate? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleTypeDate BigQuery time partitioned table's _PARTITIONDATE in YYYY-MM-DD format.
---@field projectId? string The project ID or the project number that contains the BigQuery source. Has a length limit of 128 characters. If not specified, inherits the project ID from the parent request.

---The Bigtable Options object that contains information to support the import.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptions
---@field families? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyMap The mapping from family names to an object that contains column families level information for the given column family. If a family is not present in this map it will be ignored.
---@field keyFieldName? string The field name used for saving row key value in the document. The name has to match the pattern `a-zA-Z0-9*`.

---The column of the Bigtable.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumn
---@field type? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnTypeEnum|string The type of values in this column family. The values are expected to be encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` function when the encoding value is set to `BINARY`.
---@field qualifier? string Required. Qualifier of the column. If it cannot be decoded with utf-8, use a base-64 encoded string instead.
---@field fieldName? string The field name to use for this column in the document. The name has to match the pattern `a-zA-Z0-9*`. If not set, it is parsed from the qualifier bytes with best effort. However, due to different naming patterns, field name collisions could happen, where parsing behavior is undefined.
---@field encoding? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnEncodingEnum|string The encoding mode of the values when the type is not `STRING`. Acceptable encoding values are: * `TEXT`: indicates values are alphanumeric text strings. * `BINARY`: indicates values are encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` family of functions. This can be overridden for a specific column by listing that column in `columns` and specifying an encoding for it.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnEncodingEnum "ENCODING_UNSPECIFIED"|"TEXT"|"BINARY"

---The column family of the Bigtable.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamily
---@field fieldName? string The field name to use for this column family in the document. The name has to match the pattern `a-zA-Z0-9*`. If not set, it is parsed from the family name with best effort. However, due to different naming patterns, field name collisions could happen, where parsing behavior is undefined.
---@field type? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyTypeEnum|string The type of values in this column family. The values are expected to be encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` function when the encoding value is set to `BINARY`.
---@field encoding? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyEncodingEnum|string The encoding mode of the values when the type is not STRING. Acceptable encoding values are: * `TEXT`: indicates values are alphanumeric text strings. * `BINARY`: indicates values are encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` family of functions. This can be overridden for a specific column by listing that column in `columns` and specifying an encoding for it.
---@field columns? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnList The list of objects that contains column level information for each column. If a column is not present in this list it will be ignored.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyEncodingEnum "ENCODING_UNSPECIFIED"|"TEXT"|"BINARY"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyMap { [string]: gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamily }

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STRING"|"NUMBER"|"INTEGER"|"VAR_INTEGER"|"BIG_NUMERIC"|"BOOLEAN"|"JSON"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumn[]

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptionsBigtableColumnTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STRING"|"NUMBER"|"INTEGER"|"VAR_INTEGER"|"BIG_NUMERIC"|"BOOLEAN"|"JSON"

---The Cloud Bigtable source for importing data.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableSource
---@field projectId? string The project ID that contains the Bigtable source. Has a length limit of 128 characters. If not specified, inherits the project ID from the parent request.
---@field tableId? string Required. The table ID of the Cloud Bigtable that needs to be imported.
---@field bigtableOptions? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BigtableOptions Required. Bigtable options that contains information needed when parsing data into typed structures. For example, column type annotations.
---@field instanceId? string Required. The instance ID of the Cloud Bigtable that needs to be imported.

---Response message for the GroundedGenerationService.CheckGrounding method.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CheckGroundingResponse
---@field supportScore? number The support score for the input answer candidate. Higher the score, higher is the fraction of claims that are supported by the provided facts. This is always set when a response is returned.
---@field claims? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CheckGroundingResponseClaimList Claim texts and citation info across all claims in the answer candidate.
---@field citedChunks? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FactChunkList List of facts cited across all claims in the answer candidate. These are derived from the facts supplied in the request.
---@field citedFacts? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunkList List of facts cited across all claims in the answer candidate. These are derived from the facts supplied in the request.

---Fact chunk for grounding check.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunk
---@field chunkText? string Text content of the fact chunk. Can be at most 10K characters long.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunkList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunk[]

---Text and citation info for a claim in the answer candidate.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CheckGroundingResponseClaim
---@field groundingCheckRequired? boolean Indicates that this claim required grounding check. When the system decided this claim doesn't require attribution/grounding check, this field will be set to false. In that case, no grounding check was done for the claim and therefore citation_indices should not be returned.
---@field score? number Confidence score for the claim in the answer candidate, in the range of [0, 1]. This is set only when `CheckGroundingRequest.grounding_spec.enable_claim_level_score` is true.
---@field citationIndices? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.IntegerList A list of indices (into 'cited_chunks') specifying the citations associated with the claim. For instance [1,3,4] means that cited_chunks[1], cited_chunks[3], cited_chunks[4] are the facts cited supporting for the claim. A citation to a fact indicates that the claim is supported by the fact.
---@field endPos? number Position indicating the end of the claim in the answer candidate, exclusive, in bytes. Note that this is not measured in characters and, therefore, must be rendered as such. For example, if the claim text contains non-ASCII characters, the start and end positions vary when measured in characters (programming-language-dependent) and when measured in bytes (programming-language-independent).
---@field claimText? string Text for the claim in the answer candidate. Always provided regardless of whether citations or anti-citations are found.
---@field startPos? number Position indicating the start of the claim in the answer candidate, measured in bytes. Note that this is not measured in characters and, therefore, must be rendered in the user interface keeping in mind that some characters may take more than one byte. For example, if the claim text contains non-ASCII characters, the start and end positions vary when measured in characters (programming-language-dependent) and when measured in bytes (programming-language-independent).

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CheckGroundingResponseClaimList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CheckGroundingResponseClaim[]

---Specification for the grounding check.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CheckGroundingSpec
---@field enableClaimLevelScore? boolean The control flag that enables claim-level grounding score in the response.
---@field citationThreshold? number The threshold (in [0,1]) used for determining whether a fact must be cited for a claim in the answer candidate. Choosing a higher threshold will lead to fewer but very strong citations, while choosing a lower threshold may lead to more but somewhat weaker citations. If unset, the threshold will default to 0.6.

---Chunk captures all raw metadata information of items to be recommended or searched in the chunk mode.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Chunk
---@field pageSpan? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ChunkPageSpan Page span of the chunk.
---@field content? string Content is a string from a document (parsed content).
---@field derivedStructData? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.DocumentMap Output only. This field is OUTPUT_ONLY. It contains derived data that are not in the original input document.
---@field name? string The full resource name of the chunk. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/branches/{branch}/documents/{document_id}/chunks/{chunk_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field relevanceScore? number Output only. Represents the relevance score based on similarity. Higher score indicates higher chunk relevance. The score is in range [-1.0, 1.0]. Only populated on SearchResponse.
---@field annotationMetadata? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ChunkAnnotationMetadataList Output only. The annotation metadata includes structured content in the current chunk.
---@field id? string Unique chunk ID of the current chunk.
---@field documentMetadata? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ChunkDocumentMetadata Metadata of the document from the current chunk.
---@field chunkMetadata? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ChunkChunkMetadata Output only. Metadata of the current chunk.
---@field dataUrls? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Output only. Image Data URLs if the current chunk contains images. Data URLs are composed of four parts: a prefix (data:), a MIME type indicating the type of data, an optional base64 token if non-textual, and the data itself: data:,
---@field annotationContents? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Output only. Annotation contents if the current chunk contains annotations.

---The annotation metadata includes structured content in the current chunk.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ChunkAnnotationMetadata
---@field imageId? string Output only. Image id is provided if the structured content is based on an image.
---@field structuredContent? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ChunkStructuredContent Output only. The structured content information.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ChunkAnnotationMetadataList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ChunkAnnotationMetadata[]

---Metadata of the current chunk. This field is only populated on SearchService.Search API.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ChunkChunkMetadata
---@field previousChunks? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ChunkList The previous chunks of the current chunk. The number is controlled by SearchRequest.ContentSearchSpec.ChunkSpec.num_previous_chunks. This field is only populated on SearchService.Search API.
---@field nextChunks? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ChunkList The next chunks of the current chunk. The number is controlled by SearchRequest.ContentSearchSpec.ChunkSpec.num_next_chunks. This field is only populated on SearchService.Search API.

