---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CompleteQueryResponse
---@field tailMatchTriggered? boolean True if the returned suggestions are all tail suggestions. For tail matching to be triggered, include_tail_suggestions in the request must be true and there must be no suggestions that match the full query.
---@field querySuggestions? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestionList Results of the matched query suggestions. The result list is ordered and the first result is a top suggestion.

---Suggestions as search queries.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestion
---@field suggestion? string The suggestion for the query.
---@field completableFieldPaths? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList The unique document field paths that serve as the source of this suggestion if it was generated from completable fields. This field is only populated for the document-completable model.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestionList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestion[]

---Detailed completion information including completion attribution token and clicked completion info.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CompletionInfo
---@field selectedPosition? number End user selected CompleteQueryResponse.QuerySuggestion.suggestion position, starting from 0.
---@field selectedSuggestion? string Optional. End user selected CompleteQueryResponse.QuerySuggestion.suggestion.

---Autocomplete suggestions that are imported from Customer.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CompletionSuggestion
---@field groupId? string If two suggestions have the same groupId, they will not be returned together. Instead the one ranked higher will be returned. This can be used to deduplicate semantically identical suggestions.
---@field suggestion? string Required. The suggestion text.
---@field frequency? string Frequency of this suggestion. Will be used to rank suggestions when score is not available.
---@field globalScore? number Global score of this suggestion. Control how this suggestion would be scored / ranked.
---@field groupScore? number The score of this suggestion within its group.
---@field languageCode? string BCP-47 language code of this suggestion.
---@field alternativePhrases? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Alternative matching phrases for this suggestion.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CompletionSuggestionList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CompletionSuggestion[]

---Defines circumstances to be checked before allowing a behavior
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Condition
---@field activeTimeRange? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionTimeRangeList Range of time(s) specifying when condition is active. Maximum of 10 time ranges.
---@field queryTerms? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionQueryTermList Search only A list of terms to match the query on. Cannot be set when Condition.query_regex is set. Maximum of 10 query terms.
---@field queryRegex? string Optional. Query regex to match the whole search query. Cannot be set when Condition.query_terms is set. Only supported for Basic Site Search promotion serving controls.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Condition[]

---Matcher for search request query
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionQueryTerm
---@field fullMatch? boolean Whether the search query needs to exactly match the query term.
---@field value? string The specific query value to match against Must be lowercase, must be UTF-8. Can have at most 3 space separated terms if full_match is true. Cannot be an empty string. Maximum length of 5000 characters.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionQueryTermList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionQueryTerm[]

---Used for time-dependent conditions.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionTimeRange
---@field startTime? string Start of time range. Range is inclusive.
---@field endTime? string End of time range. Range is inclusive. Must be in the future.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionTimeRangeList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionTimeRange[]

---Defines a conditioned behavior to employ during serving. Must be attached to a ServingConfig to be considered at serving time. Permitted actions dependent on `SolutionType`.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Control
---@field redirectAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlRedirectAction Defines a redirect-type control.
---@field associatedServingConfigIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Output only. List of all ServingConfig IDs this control is attached to. May take up to 10 minutes to update after changes.
---@field conditions? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionList Determines when the associated action will trigger. Omit to always apply the action. Currently only a single condition may be specified. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field useCases? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlUseCasesItemEnumList Specifies the use case for the control. Affects what condition fields can be set. Only applies to SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH. Currently only allow one use case per control. Must be set when solution_type is SolutionType.SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlSolutionTypeEnum Required. Immutable. What solution the control belongs to. Must be compatible with vertical of resource. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field name? string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/*/locations/global/dataStore/*/controls/*`
---@field displayName? string Required. Human readable name. The identifier used in UI views. Must be UTF-8 encoded string. Length limit is 128 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field boostAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostAction Defines a boost-type control
---@field synonymsAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlSynonymsAction Treats a group of terms as synonyms of one another.
---@field filterAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlFilterAction Defines a filter-type control Currently not supported by Recommendation
---@field promoteAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlPromoteAction Promote certain links based on predefined trigger queries.

---Adjusts order of products in returned list.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostAction
---@field interpolationBoostSpec? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpec Optional. Complex specification for custom ranking based on customer defined attribute value.
---@field filter? string Required. Specifies which products to apply the boost to. If no filter is provided all products will be boosted (No-op). Syntax documentation: https://cloud.google.com/retail/docs/filter-and-order Maximum length is 5000 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field fixedBoost? number Optional. Strength of the boost, which should be in [-1, 1]. Negative boost means demotion. Default is 0.0 (No-op).
---@field dataStore? string Required. Specifies which data store's documents can be boosted by this control. Full data store name e.g. projects/123/locations/global/collections/default_collection/dataStores/default_data_store
---@field boost? number Strength of the boost, which should be in [-1, 1]. Negative boost means demotion. Default is 0.0 (No-op).

---Specification for custom ranking based on customer specified attribute value. It provides more controls for customized ranking than the simple (condition, boost) combination above.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpec
---@field fieldName? string Optional. The name of the field whose value will be used to determine the boost amount.
---@field controlPoints? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPointList Optional. The control points used to define the curve. The monotonic function (defined through the interpolation_type above) passes through the control points listed here.
---@field attributeType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecAttributeTypeEnum|string Optional. The attribute type to be used to determine the boost amount. The attribute value can be derived from the field value of the specified field_name. In the case of numerical it is straightforward i.e. attribute_value = numerical_field_value. In the case of freshness however, attribute_value = (time.now() - datetime_field_value).
---@field interpolationType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecInterpolationTypeEnum|string Optional. The interpolation type to be applied to connect the control points listed below.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecAttributeTypeEnum "ATTRIBUTE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NUMERICAL"|"FRESHNESS"

---The control points used to define the curve. The curve defined through these control points can only be monotonically increasing or decreasing(constant values are acceptable).
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPoint
---@field boostAmount? number Optional. The value between -1 to 1 by which to boost the score if the attribute_value evaluates to the value specified above.
---@field attributeValue? string Optional. Can be one of: 1. The numerical field value. 2. The duration spec for freshness: The value must be formatted as an XSD `dayTimeDuration` value (a restricted subset of an ISO 8601 duration value). The pattern for this is: `nDnM]`.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPointList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPoint[]

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecInterpolationTypeEnum "INTERPOLATION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"LINEAR"

---Specified which products may be included in results. Uses same filter as boost.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlFilterAction
---@field filter? string Required. A filter to apply on the matching condition results. Required Syntax documentation: https://cloud.google.com/retail/docs/filter-and-order Maximum length is 5000 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field dataStore? string Required. Specifies which data store's documents can be filtered by this control. Full data store name e.g. projects/123/locations/global/collections/default_collection/dataStores/default_data_store

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Control[]

---Promote certain links based on some trigger queries. Example: Promote shoe store link when searching for `shoe` keyword. The link can be outside of associated data store.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlPromoteAction
---@field searchLinkPromotion? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SearchLinkPromotion Required. Promotion attached to this action.
---@field dataStore? string Required. Data store with which this promotion is attached to.

---Redirects a shopper to the provided URI.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlRedirectAction
---@field redirectUri? string Required. The URI to which the shopper will be redirected. Required. URI must have length equal or less than 2000 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlSolutionTypeEnum "SOLUTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_GENERATIVE_CHAT"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_AI_MODE"

---Creates a set of terms that will act as synonyms of one another. Example: "happy" will also be considered as "glad", "glad" will also be considered as "happy".
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlSynonymsAction
---@field synonyms? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Defines a set of synonyms. Can specify up to 100 synonyms. Must specify at least 2 synonyms. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlUseCasesItemEnum "SEARCH_USE_CASE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SEARCH_USE_CASE_SEARCH"|"SEARCH_USE_CASE_BROWSE"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlUseCasesItemEnumList (gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlUseCasesItemEnum|string)[]

---External conversation proto definition.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Conversation
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the conversation started.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the conversation finished.
---@field messages? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationMessageList Conversation messages.
---@field state? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationStateEnum|string The state of the Conversation.
---@field userPseudoId? string A unique identifier for tracking users.
---@field name? string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/dataStore/*/conversations/*` or `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/*/conversations/*`.

---Defines context of the conversation
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationContext
---@field activeDocument? string The current active document the user opened. It contains the document resource reference.
---@field contextDocuments? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList The current list of documents the user is seeing. It contains the document resource references.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Conversation[]

---Defines a conversation message.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationMessage
---@field createTime? string Output only. Message creation timestamp.
---@field userInput? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1TextInput User text input.
---@field reply? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Reply Search reply.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationMessageList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationMessage[]

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"IN_PROGRESS"|"COMPLETED"

---Response message for ConversationalSearchService.ConverseConversation method.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConverseConversationResponse
---@field reply? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Reply Answer to the current query.
---@field searchResults? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SearchResponseSearchResultList Search Results.
---@field conversation? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Conversation Updated conversation including the answer.

---Request message for SiteSearchEngineService.CreateTargetSite method.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CreateTargetSiteRequest
---@field targetSite? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1TargetSite Required. The TargetSite to create.
---@field parent? string Required. Parent resource name of TargetSite, such as `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/siteSearchEngine`.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CreateTargetSiteRequestList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CreateTargetSiteRequest[]

---A custom attribute that is not explicitly modeled in a resource, e.g. UserEvent.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CustomAttribute
---@field numbers? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.DoubleList The numerical values of this custom attribute. For example, `[2.3, 15.4]` when the key is "lengths_cm". Exactly one of CustomAttribute.text or CustomAttribute.numbers should be set. Otherwise, an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is returned.
---@field text? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList The textual values of this custom attribute. For example, `["yellow", "green"]` when the key is "color". Empty string is not allowed. Otherwise, an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is returned. Exactly one of CustomAttribute.text or CustomAttribute.numbers should be set. Otherwise, an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is returned.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CustomAttributeMap { [string]: gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CustomAttribute }

---Metadata that describes a custom tuned model.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CustomTuningModel
---@field name? string Required. The fully qualified resource name of the model. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/customTuningModels/{custom_tuning_model}`. Model must be an alpha-numerical string with limit of 40 characters.
---@field errorMessage? string Currently this is only populated if the model state is `INPUT_VALIDATION_FAILED`.
---@field metrics? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.DoubleMap The metrics of the trained model.
---@field modelVersion? string The version of the model.
---@field trainingStartTime? string Timestamp the model training was initiated.
---@field displayName? string The display name of the model.
---@field modelState? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CustomTuningModelModelStateEnum The state that the model is in (e.g.`TRAINING` or `TRAINING_FAILED`).
---@field createTime? string Deprecated: Timestamp the Model was created at.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CustomTuningModelList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CustomTuningModel[]

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CustomTuningModelModelStateEnum "MODEL_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"TRAINING_PAUSED"|"TRAINING"|"TRAINING_COMPLETE"|"READY_FOR_SERVING"|"TRAINING_FAILED"|"NO_IMPROVEMENT"|"INPUT_VALIDATION_FAILED"

---Manages the connection to external data sources for all data stores grouped under a Collection. It's a singleton resource of Collection. The initialization is only supported through DataConnectorService.SetUpDataConnector method, which will create a new Collection and initialize its DataConnector.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnector
---@field connectorModes? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorConnectorModesItemEnumList Optional. The modes enabled for this connector. Default state is CONNECTOR_MODE_UNSPECIFIED.
---@field dataSource? string Required. The identifier for the data source. For the full, up-to-date list of supported connectors and their values, see [Connect a third-party data source](https://docs.cloud.google.com/gemini/enterprise/docs/connectors/connect-third-party-data-source#sources-by-launch-stage).
---@field staticIpEnabled? boolean Optional. Whether customer has enabled static IP addresses for this connector.
---@field oauthStaticIpAddresses? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Output only. The static IP addresses used by this connector for OAuth APIs (e.g. end user authentication). These are surfaced separately from `static_ip_addresses` so that customers can apply granular firewall settings for OAuth endpoints. Only populated for connectors that have static IP enabled and are used for actions and/or federated search.
---@field syncMode? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorSyncModeEnum|string The data synchronization mode supported by the data connector.
---@field errors? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleRpcStatusList Output only. The errors from initialization or from the latest connector run.
---@field connectorSourceId? string Optional. If set, this value instead of `data_source` is used to fetch the corresponding connector source.
---@field metadata? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorConnectorMetadata Optional. User-facing metadata for the connector. Populated from the connector's generated metadata / registry `ConnectorSource`.
---@field removeParamKeys? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. Specifies keys to be removed from the 'params' field. This is only active when 'params' is included in the 'update_mask' in an UpdateDataConnectorRequest. Deletion takes precedence if a key is both in 'remove_param_keys' and present in the 'params' field of the request.
---@field identityScheduleConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1IdentityScheduleConfig The configuration for the identity data synchronization runs. This contains the refresh interval to sync the Access Control List information for the documents ingested by this connector.
---@field refreshInterval? string Required. The refresh interval for data sync. If duration is set to 0, the data will be synced in real time. The streaming feature is not supported yet. The minimum is 30 minutes and maximum is 7 days. When the refresh interval is set to the same value as the incremental refresh interval, incremental sync will be disabled.
---@field dynamicTools? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DynamicToolList Output only. The dynamic tools fetched for this connector.
---@field state? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorStateEnum|string Output only. State of the connector.
---@field entities? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorSourceEntityList List of entities from the connected data source to ingest.
---@field lastSyncTime? string Output only. For periodic connectors only, the last time a data sync was completed.
---@field vpcscEnabled? boolean Output only. Whether the connector is created with VPC-SC enabled.
---@field autoRunDisabled? boolean Optional. Indicates whether the connector is disabled for auto run. It can be used to pause periodical and real time sync. Update: with the introduction of incremental_sync_disabled, auto_run_disabled is used to pause/disable only full syncs
---@field federatedConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorFederatedConfig Optional. Any params and credentials used specifically for hybrid connectors supporting FEDERATED mode. This field should only be set if the connector is a hybrid connector and we want to enable FEDERATED mode.
---@field staticIpAddresses? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Output only. The static IP addresses used by this connector.
---@field incrementalRefreshInterval? string Optional. The refresh interval specifically for incremental data syncs. If unset, incremental syncs will use the default from env, set to 3hrs. The minimum is 30 minutes and maximum is 7 days. Applicable to only 3P connectors. When the refresh interval is set to the same value as the incremental refresh interval, incremental sync will be disabled.
---@field incrementalSyncDisabled? boolean Optional. Indicates whether incremental syncs are paused for this connector. This is independent of auto_run_disabled. Applicable to only 3P connectors. When the refresh interval is set to the same value as the incremental refresh interval, incremental sync will be disabled, i.e. set to true.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the DataConnector was last updated.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the DataConnector was created at.
---@field endUserConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorEndUserConfig Optional. Any params and credentials used specifically for EUA connectors.
---@field kmsKeyName? string Input only. The KMS key to be used to protect the DataStores managed by this connector. Must be set for requests that need to comply with CMEK Org Policy protections. If this field is set and processed successfully, the DataStores created by this connector will be protected by the KMS key.
---@field cliConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CliConfig Optional. The configuration for establishing a CLI connection.
---@field jsonParams? string Required data connector parameters in json string format.
---@field tag? string Optional. Immutable. User-facing, version-independent label for this connector. May be shared by multiple connectors under the same (project, location, collection, data_source); tag-based lookup returns the one with the greatest create_time. Optional at Create time. If the caller omits `tag`, the server auto-derives one from the collection_id (falling back to data_source, else a time-based `t-` sentinel). The auto-derived tag is subject to the same immutability guarantee as a caller-supplied one, so callers who care about the exact tag value should provide it explicitly rather than relying on the server default. Agent Designer resolves connectors via (data_source, tag) when set, falling back to the legacy resource-name lookup when unset, so connectors created before the tag-write launch continue to work without a backfill.
---@field latestPauseTime? string Output only. The most recent timestamp when this DataConnector was paused, affecting all functionalities such as data synchronization. Pausing a connector has the following effects: - All functionalities, including data synchronization, are halted. - Any ongoing data synchronization job will be canceled. - No future data synchronization runs will be scheduled nor can be triggered.
---@field hybridIngestionDisabled? boolean Optional. If the connector is a hybrid connector, determines whether ingestion is enabled and appropriate resources are provisioned during connector creation. If the connector is not a hybrid connector, this field is ignored.
---@field destinationConfigs? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DestinationConfigList Optional. Any target destinations used to connect to third-party services.
---@field dataProtectionPolicy? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataProtectionPolicy Optional. Specifies the data protection policy for the connector.
---@field bapConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1BAPConfig Optional. The configuration for establishing a BAP connection.
---@field egressFqdns? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Output only. The list of FQDNs of the data connector can egress to. This includes both FQDN derived from the customer provided instance URL and default per connector type FQDNs.
---@field realtimeSyncConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorRealtimeSyncConfig Optional. The configuration for realtime sync.
---@field blockingReasons? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorBlockingReasonsItemEnumList Output only. User actions that must be completed before the connector can start syncing data.
---@field realtimeState? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorRealtimeStateEnum|string Output only. real-time sync state
---@field connectorType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorConnectorTypeEnum|string Output only. The type of connector. Each source can only map to one type. For example, salesforce, confluence and jira have THIRD_PARTY connector type. It is not mutable once set by system.
---@field privateConnectivityProjectId? string Output only. The tenant project ID associated with private connectivity connectors. This project must be allowlisted by in order for the connector to function.
---@field alertPolicyConfigs? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AlertPolicyConfigList Optional. The connector level alert config.
---@field createEuaSaas? boolean Optional. Whether the END USER AUTHENTICATION connector is created in SaaS.
---@field params? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.DocumentMap Required data connector parameters in structured json format.
---@field name? string Identifier. The full resource name of the Data Connector. Format: `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/dataConnector`.
---@field actionState? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorActionStateEnum|string Output only. State of the action connector. This reflects whether the action connector is initializing, active or has encountered errors.
---@field aclEnabled? boolean Optional. Whether the connector will be created with an ACL config. Currently this field only affects Cloud Storage and BigQuery connectors.
---@field actionConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ActionConfig Optional. Action configurations to make the connector support actions.
---@field identityRefreshInterval? string The refresh interval to sync the Access Control List information for the documents ingested by this connector. If not set, the access control list will be refreshed at the default interval of 30 minutes. The identity refresh interval can be at least 30 minutes and at most 7 days.
---@field nextSyncTime? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleTypeDateTime Defines the scheduled time for the next data synchronization. This field requires hour , minute, and time_zone from the [IANA Time Zone Database](https://www.iana.org/time-zones). This is utilized when the data connector has a refresh interval greater than 1 day. When the hours or minutes are not specified, we will assume a sync time of 0:00. The user must provide a time zone to avoid ambiguity.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorActionStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CREATING"|"ACTIVE"|"FAILED"|"RUNNING"|"WARNING"|"INITIALIZATION_FAILED"|"UPDATING"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorBlockingReasonsItemEnum "BLOCKING_REASON_UNSPECIFIED"|"ALLOWLIST_STATIC_IP"|"ALLOWLIST_IN_SERVICE_ATTACHMENT"|"ALLOWLIST_SERVICE_ACCOUNT"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorBlockingReasonsItemEnumList (gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorBlockingReasonsItemEnum|string)[]

---User-facing metadata for the connector, shown on the connector detail page (title, description, short_description, author, note).
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataConnectorConnectorMetadata
---@field description? string Optional. Human-readable description of the connector, shown on the connector detail page. One connector has a single description.
---@field shortDescription? string Optional. Short, subtitle-length description of the connector (e.g. shown beneath the connector name in list and detail views).
---@field author? string Optional. The party that authored the connector, e.g. "Google" or a third-party provider name. Lets end users see who authored a connector.
---@field note? string Optional. Free-form, multi-line note about the connector's capabilities or a custom note that can be set for the connector.
---@field title? string Optional. Display title of the connector.

