---Document captures all raw metadata information of items to be recommended or searched.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Document
---@field parentDocumentId? string The identifier of the parent document. Currently supports at most two level document hierarchy. Id should conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) standard with a length limit of 63 characters.
---@field derivedStructData? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.DocumentMap Output only. This field is OUTPUT_ONLY. It contains derived data that are not in the original input document.
---@field indexStatus? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentIndexStatus Output only. The index status of the document. * If document is indexed successfully, the index_time field is populated. * Otherwise, if document is not indexed due to errors, the error_samples field is populated. * Otherwise, if document's index is in progress, the pending_message field is populated.
---@field id? string Immutable. The identifier of the document. Id should conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) standard with a length limit of 128 characters.
---@field structData? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.DocumentMap The structured JSON data for the document. It should conform to the registered Schema or an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is thrown.
---@field jsonData? string The JSON string representation of the document. It should conform to the registered Schema or an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is thrown.
---@field content? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentContent The unstructured data linked to this document. Content can only be set and must be set if this document is under a `CONTENT_REQUIRED` data store.
---@field indexTime? string Output only. The time when the document was last indexed. If this field is populated, it means the document has been indexed. While documents typically become searchable within seconds of indexing, it can sometimes take up to a few hours. If this field is not populated, it means the document has never been indexed.
---@field schemaId? string The identifier of the schema located in the same data store.
---@field aclInfo? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentAclInfo Access control information for the document.
---@field name? string Immutable. The full resource name of the document. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/branches/{branch}/documents/{document_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.

---ACL Information of the Document.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentAclInfo
---@field readers? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentAclInfoAccessRestrictionList Readers of the document.

---AclRestriction to model complex inheritance restrictions. Example: Modeling a "Both Permit" inheritance, where to access a child document, user needs to have access to parent document. Document Hierarchy - Space_S --> Page_P. Readers: Space_S: group_1, user_1 Page_P: group_2, group_3, user_2 Space_S ACL Restriction - { "acl_info": { "readers": [ { "principals": [ { "group_id": "group_1" }, { "user_id": "user_1" } ] } ] } } Page_P ACL Restriction. { "acl_info": { "readers": [ { "principals": [ { "group_id": "group_2" }, { "group_id": "group_3" }, { "user_id": "user_2" } ], }, { "principals": [ { "group_id": "group_1" }, { "user_id": "user_1" } ], } ] } }
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentAclInfoAccessRestriction
---@field principals? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1PrincipalList List of principals.
---@field idpWide? boolean All users within the Identity Provider.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentAclInfoAccessRestrictionList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentAclInfoAccessRestriction[]

---Unstructured data linked to this document.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentContent
---@field rawBytes? string The content represented as a stream of bytes. The maximum length is 1,000,000 bytes (1 MB / ~0.95 MiB). Note: As with all `bytes` fields, this field is represented as pure binary in Protocol Buffers and base64-encoded string in JSON. For example, `abc123!?$*&()'-=@~` should be represented as `YWJjMTIzIT8kKiYoKSctPUB+` in JSON. See https://developers.google.com/protocol-buffers/docs/proto3#json.
---@field uri? string The URI of the content. Only Cloud Storage URIs (e.g. `gs://bucket-name/path/to/file`) are supported. The maximum file size is 2.5 MB for text-based formats, 200 MB for other formats.
---@field mimeType? string The MIME type of the content. Supported types: * `application/pdf` (PDF, only native PDFs are supported for now) * `text/html` (HTML) * `text/plain` (TXT) * `application/xml` or `text/xml` (XML) * `application/json` (JSON) * `application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document` (DOCX) * `application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation` (PPTX) * `application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet` (XLSX) * `application/vnd.ms-excel.sheet.macroenabled.12` (XLSM) The following types are supported only if layout parser is enabled in the data store: * `image/bmp` (BMP) * `image/gif` (GIF) * `image/jpeg` (JPEG) * `image/png` (PNG) * `image/tiff` (TIFF) See https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml.

---Index status of the document.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentIndexStatus
---@field indexTime? string The time when the document was indexed. If this field is populated, it means the document has been indexed. While documents typically become searchable within seconds of indexing, it can sometimes take up to a few hours.
---@field errorSamples? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleRpcStatusList A sample of errors encountered while indexing the document. If this field is populated, the document is not indexed due to errors.
---@field pendingMessage? string Immutable. The message indicates the document index is in progress. If this field is populated, the document index is pending.

---Detailed document information associated with a user event.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentInfo
---@field conversionValue? number Optional. The conversion value associated with this Document. Must be set if UserEvent.event_type is "conversion". For example, a value of 1000 signifies that 1000 seconds were spent viewing a Document for the `watch` conversion type.
---@field joined? boolean Output only. Whether the referenced Document can be found in the data store.
---@field name? string The Document resource full name, of the form: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}/branches/{branch_id}/documents/{document_id}`
---@field uri? string The Document URI - only allowed for website data stores.
---@field promotionIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList The promotion IDs associated with this Document. Currently, this field is restricted to at most one ID.
---@field quantity? number Quantity of the Document associated with the user event. Defaults to 1. For example, this field is 2 if two quantities of the same Document are involved in a `add-to-cart` event. Required for events of the following event types: * `add-to-cart` * `purchase`
---@field id? string The Document resource ID.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentInfoList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentInfo[]

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Document[]

---A singleton resource of DataStore. If it's empty when DataStore is created and DataStore is set to DataStore.ContentConfig.CONTENT_REQUIRED, the default parser will default to digital parser.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfig
---@field defaultParsingConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfig Configurations for default Document parser. If not specified, we will configure it as default DigitalParsingConfig, and the default parsing config will be applied to all file types for Document parsing.
---@field parsingConfigOverrides? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigMap Map from file type to override the default parsing configuration based on the file type. Supported keys: * `pdf`: Override parsing config for PDF files, either digital parsing, ocr parsing or layout parsing is supported. * `html`: Override parsing config for HTML files, only digital parsing and layout parsing are supported. * `docx`: Override parsing config for DOCX files, only digital parsing and layout parsing are supported. * `pptx`: Override parsing config for PPTX files, only digital parsing and layout parsing are supported. * `xlsm`: Override parsing config for XLSM files, only digital parsing and layout parsing are supported. * `xlsx`: Override parsing config for XLSX files, only digital parsing and layout parsing are supported.
---@field chunkingConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigChunkingConfig Whether chunking mode is enabled.
---@field name? string The full resource name of the Document Processing Config. Format: `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/dataStores/*/documentProcessingConfig`.

---Configuration for chunking config.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigChunkingConfig
---@field layoutBasedChunkingConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigChunkingConfigLayoutBasedChunkingConfig Configuration for the layout based chunking.

---Configuration for the layout based chunking.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigChunkingConfigLayoutBasedChunkingConfig
---@field chunkSize? number The token size limit for each chunk. Supported values: 100-500 (inclusive). Default value: 500.
---@field includeAncestorHeadings? boolean Whether to include appending different levels of headings to chunks from the middle of the document to prevent context loss. Default value: False.

---Related configurations applied to a specific type of document parser.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfig
---@field layoutParsingConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigLayoutParsingConfig Configurations applied to layout parser.
---@field digitalParsingConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigDigitalParsingConfig Configurations applied to digital parser.
---@field ocrParsingConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigOcrParsingConfig Configurations applied to OCR parser. Currently it only applies to PDFs.

---The digital parsing configurations for documents.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigDigitalParsingConfig

---The layout parsing configurations for documents.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfigParsingConfigLayoutParsingConfig
---@field enableGetProcessedDocument? boolean Optional. If true, the processed document will be made available for the GetProcessedDocument API.
---@field enableImageAnnotation? boolean Optional. If true, the LLM based annotation is added to the image during parsing.
---@field excludeHtmlClasses? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. List of HTML classes to exclude from the parsed content.
---@field excludeHtmlElements? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. List of HTML elements to exclude from the parsed content.
---@field enableTableAnnotation? boolean Optional. If true, the LLM based annotation is added to the table during parsing.
---@field enableLlmLayoutParsing? boolean Optional. If true, the pdf layout will be refined using an LLM.
---@field excludeHtmlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. List of HTML ids to exclude from the parsed content.
---@field structuredContentTypes? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. Contains the required structure types to extract from the document. Supported values: * `shareholder-structure`

