---Metadata that describes the training and serving parameters of an Engine.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Engine
---@field cmekConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CmekConfig Output only. CMEK-related information for the Engine.
---@field chatEngineMetadata? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineChatEngineMetadata Output only. Additional information of the Chat Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineIndustryVerticalEnum Optional. The industry vertical that the engine registers. The restriction of the Engine industry vertical is based on DataStore: Vertical on Engine has to match vertical of the DataStore linked to the engine.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Recommendation Engine was last updated.
---@field searchEngineConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfig Configurations for the Search Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Recommendation Engine was created at.
---@field sessionConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SessionConfig Optional. Non-empty default. Session config for the engine.
---@field connectorTenantInfo? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringMap Optional. Maps a connector ID (e.g., "hybrid-github", "shopify") to tenant-specific information required for that connector. The structure of the tenant information string is connector-dependent.
---@field modelConfigs? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineModelConfigsValueEnumMap Optional. Maps a model name to its specific configuration for this engine. This allows admin users to turn on/off individual models. This only stores models whose states are overridden by the admin. When the state is unspecified, or model_configs is empty for this model, the system will decide if this model should be available or not based on the default configuration. For example, a preview model should be disabled by default if the admin has not chosen to enable it.
---@field effectiveFeatures? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineEffectiveFeaturesValueEnumMap Output only. The complete, server-resolved state of every known feature toggle. Unlike `features`, which stores only explicit admin overrides, this map always contains an entry for every toggle. Clients should read toggle state from this field.
---@field associatedAgentRegistry? string Output only. The Agent registry containing the agents, MCP servers and tools associated with this engine. Derived server-side from the linked Agent Gateway's registry.
---@field observabilityConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ObservabilityConfig Optional. Observability config for the engine.
---@field chatEngineConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineChatEngineConfig Configurations for the Chat Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT.
---@field features? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturesValueEnumMap Optional. Feature config for the engine to opt in or opt out of features. Supported keys: * `*`: all features, if it's present, all other feature state settings are ignored. * `agent-gallery` * `no-code-agent-builder` * `prompt-gallery` * `model-selector` * `notebook-lm` * `people-search` * `people-search-org-chart` * `bi-directional-audio` * `speech-to-text` * `feedback` * `session-sharing` * `personalization-memory` * `personalization-suggested-highlights` * `mobile-app-access` * `disable-agent-sharing` * `disable-image-generation` * `disable-video-generation` * `music-generation` * `speech-generation` * `disable-onedrive-upload` * `disable-talk-to-content` * `disable-google-drive-upload` * `disable-welcome-emails` * `disable-canvas` * `canvas-workspace` * `canvas-app-builder` * `skills` * `skill-sharing` * `skill-sharing-without-admin-approval` * `skill-security-scan` * `disable-projects` * `sobi` * `enable-end-user-sharing-with-groups` * `single-agent-orchestration` * `multi-agent-orchestration` * `cross-product-intelligence` * `workflow-agents` * `in-app-notifications` * `code-extraction` * `remote-vm` * `license-tier-badge` * `canvas-app-sharing` * `agent-marketplace` * `agent-scheduling` * `preview-agents` * `plugins`
---@field globalFeatureToggleState? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineGlobalFeatureToggleStateEnum Optional. Controls the global feature toggle state for the engine.
---@field delayedGlobalFeatureToggleStateAllowed? boolean Output only. Whether the project is allowed to set `global_feature_toggle_state` to `DELAYED`.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the engine. Should be human readable. UTF-8 encoded string with limit of 1024 characters.
---@field procurementContactEmails? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. The emails of the procurement contacts.
---@field dataStoreIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. The data stores associated with this engine. For SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH and SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION type of engines, they can only associate with at most one data store. If solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT, multiple DataStores in the same Collection can be associated here. Note that when used in CreateEngineRequest, one DataStore id must be provided as the system will use it for necessary initializations.
---@field marketplaceAgentVisibility? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMarketplaceAgentVisibilityEnum Optional. The visibility of marketplace agents in the agent gallery.
---@field featurePolicies? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMap Optional. Per-feature access policies, keyed by feature toggle name (see `features`). A feature with no entry is available to every user when it is on. Only features that support access policies are accepted.
---@field mediaRecommendationEngineConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfig Configurations for the Media Engine. Only applicable on the data stores with solution_type SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION and IndustryVertical.MEDIA vertical.
---@field knowledgeGraphConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineKnowledgeGraphConfig Optional. Configurations for the Knowledge Graph. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field agentGatewaySetting? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AgentGatewaySetting Optional. The agent gateway setting for the engine.
---@field name? string Immutable. Identifier. The fully qualified resource name of the engine. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}` engine should be 1-63 characters, and valid characters are /a-z0-9*/. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field commonConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineCommonConfig Common config spec that specifies the metadata of the engine.
---@field disableAnalytics? boolean Optional. Whether to disable analytics for searches performed on this engine.
---@field appType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineAppTypeEnum Optional. Immutable. This the application type which this engine resource represents. NOTE: this is a new concept independ of existing industry vertical or solution type.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSolutionTypeEnum Required. The solutions of the engine.
---@field configurableBillingApproach? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineConfigurableBillingApproachEnum Optional. Configuration for configurable billing approach.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineAppTypeEnum "APP_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"APP_TYPE_INTRANET"

---Configurations for a Chat Engine.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineChatEngineConfig
---@field agentCreationConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineChatEngineConfigAgentCreationConfig The configurationt generate the Dialogflow agent that is associated to this Engine. Note that these configurations are one-time consumed by and passed to Dialogflow service. It means they cannot be retrieved using EngineService.GetEngine or EngineService.ListEngines API after engine creation.
---@field allowCrossRegion? boolean Optional. If the flag set to true, we allow the agent and engine are in different locations, otherwise the agent and engine are required to be in the same location. The flag is set to false by default. Note that the `allow_cross_region` are one-time consumed by and passed to EngineService.CreateEngine. It means they cannot be retrieved using EngineService.GetEngine or EngineService.ListEngines API after engine creation.
---@field dialogflowAgentToLink? string The resource name of an exist Dialogflow agent to link to this Chat Engine. Customers can either provide `agent_creation_config` to create agent or provide an agent name that links the agent with the Chat engine. Format: `projects//locations//agents/`. Note that the `dialogflow_agent_to_link` are one-time consumed by and passed to Dialogflow service. It means they cannot be retrieved using EngineService.GetEngine or EngineService.ListEngines API after engine creation. Use ChatEngineMetadata.dialogflow_agent for actual agent association after Engine is created.

---Configurations for generating a Dialogflow agent. Note that these configurations are one-time consumed by and passed to Dialogflow service. It means they cannot be retrieved using EngineService.GetEngine or EngineService.ListEngines API after engine creation.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineChatEngineConfigAgentCreationConfig
---@field timeZone? string Required. The time zone of the agent from the [time zone database](https://www.iana.org/time-zones), e.g., America/New_York, Europe/Paris.
---@field location? string Agent location for Agent creation, supported values: global/us/eu. If not provided, us Engine will create Agent using us-central-1 by default; eu Engine will create Agent using eu-west-1 by default.
---@field defaultLanguageCode? string Required. The default language of the agent as a language tag. See [Language Support](https://cloud.google.com/dialogflow/docs/reference/language) for a list of the currently supported language codes.
---@field business? string Name of the company, organization or other entity that the agent represents. Used for knowledge connector LLM prompt and for knowledge search.

---Additional information of a Chat Engine. Fields in this message are output only.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineChatEngineMetadata
---@field dialogflowAgent? string The resource name of a Dialogflow agent, that this Chat Engine refers to. Format: `projects//locations//agents/`.

---Common configurations for an Engine.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineCommonConfig
---@field companyName? string The name of the company, business or entity that is associated with the engine. Setting this may help improve LLM related features.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineConfigurableBillingApproachEnum "CONFIGURABLE_BILLING_APPROACH_UNSPECIFIED"|"CONFIGURABLE_BILLING_APPROACH_ENABLED"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineEffectiveFeaturesValueEnum "FEATURE_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"FEATURE_STATE_ON"|"FEATURE_STATE_OFF"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineEffectiveFeaturesValueEnumMap { [string]: gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineEffectiveFeaturesValueEnum|string }

---Restricts which users may use a feature that is turned on in `features`.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicy
---@field defaultAccess? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyDefaultAccessEnum|string Optional. Access for users who match neither list.
---@field deniedMembers? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMemberList Optional. Members who may not use the feature. Takes precedence over `allowed_members`.
---@field allowedMembers? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMemberList Optional. Members who may use the feature.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyDefaultAccessEnum "DEFAULT_ACCESS_UNSPECIFIED"|"ALLOW"|"DENY"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMap { [string]: gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicy }

---A user or group the policy refers to.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMember
---@field id? string Required. Identifier evaluated at serving time. Its format depends on the project's identity provider: * Google identity (`GSUITE`): the group or user email. For groups, the server resolves the email to a group ID on write and returns the email on read. * Workforce Identity Federation (`THIRD_PARTY`), groups: the value the provider emits in `google.groups`. With SCIM this is the SCIM group ID; without SCIM and with the default Microsoft Entra mapping it is the Entra group object ID. * Workforce Identity Federation, users: the user's workforce identity subject.
---@field displayName? string Optional. Label shown in the console. Never used for evaluation.
---@field verification? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMemberVerificationEnum|string Output only. Result of the server's directory check when the member was saved.
---@field type? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMemberTypeEnum|string Required. Kind of member.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMemberList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMember[]

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMemberTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"USER"|"GROUP"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMemberVerificationEnum "VERIFICATION_UNSPECIFIED"|"VERIFIED"|"NOT_FOUND"|"NOT_VERIFIABLE"|"CHECK_FAILED"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturesValueEnum "FEATURE_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"FEATURE_STATE_ON"|"FEATURE_STATE_OFF"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturesValueEnumMap { [string]: gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturesValueEnum|string }

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineGlobalFeatureToggleStateEnum "GLOBAL_FEATURE_TOGGLE_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DELAYED"|"SCHEDULED"|"GENERAL"|"EARLY"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineIndustryVerticalEnum "INDUSTRY_VERTICAL_UNSPECIFIED"|"GENERIC"|"MEDIA"|"HEALTHCARE_FHIR"

---Configuration message for the Knowledge Graph.
