---Additional config specs for a Media Recommendation engine.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfig
---@field optimizationObjectiveConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfigOptimizationObjectiveConfig Name and value of the custom threshold for cvr optimization_objective. For target_field `watch-time`, target_field_value must be an integer value indicating the media progress time in seconds between (0, 86400] (excludes 0, includes 86400) (e.g., 90). For target_field `watch-percentage`, the target_field_value must be a valid float value between (0, 1.0] (excludes 0, includes 1.0) (e.g., 0.5).
---@field type? string Required. The type of engine. e.g., `recommended-for-you`. This field together with optimization_objective describe engine metadata to use to control engine training and serving. Currently supported values: `recommended-for-you`, `others-you-may-like`, `more-like-this`, `most-popular-items`.
---@field engineFeaturesConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfigEngineFeaturesConfig Optional. Additional engine features config.
---@field trainingState? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfigTrainingStateEnum|string The training state that the engine is in (e.g. `TRAINING` or `PAUSED`). Since part of the cost of running the service is frequency of training - this can be used to determine when to train engine in order to control cost. If not specified: the default value for `CreateEngine` method is `TRAINING`. The default value for `UpdateEngine` method is to keep the state the same as before.
---@field optimizationObjective? string The optimization objective. e.g., `cvr`. This field together with optimization_objective describe engine metadata to use to control engine training and serving. Currently supported values: `ctr`, `cvr`. If not specified, we choose default based on engine type. Default depends on type of recommendation: `recommended-for-you` => `ctr` `others-you-may-like` => `ctr`

---More feature configs of the selected engine type.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfigEngineFeaturesConfig
---@field recommendedForYouConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfigRecommendedForYouFeatureConfig Recommended for you engine feature config.
---@field mostPopularConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfigMostPopularFeatureConfig Most popular engine feature config.

---Feature configurations that are required for creating a Most Popular engine.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfigMostPopularFeatureConfig
---@field timeWindowDays? string The time window of which the engine is queried at training and prediction time. Positive integers only. The value translates to the last X days of events. Currently required for the `most-popular-items` engine.

---Custom threshold for `cvr` optimization_objective.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfigOptimizationObjectiveConfig
---@field targetField? string Required. The name of the field to target. Currently supported values: `watch-percentage`, `watch-time`.
---@field targetFieldValueFloat? number Required. The threshold to be applied to the target (e.g., 0.5).

---Additional feature configurations for creating a `recommended-for-you` engine.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfigRecommendedForYouFeatureConfig
---@field contextEventType? string The type of event with which the engine is queried at prediction time. If set to `generic`, only `view-item`, `media-play`,and `media-complete` will be used as `context-event` in engine training. If set to `view-home-page`, `view-home-page` will also be used as `context-events` in addition to `view-item`, `media-play`, and `media-complete`. Currently supported for the `recommended-for-you` engine. Currently supported values: `view-home-page`, `generic`.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfigTrainingStateEnum "TRAINING_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PAUSED"|"TRAINING"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineModelConfigsValueEnum "MODEL_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"MODEL_ENABLED"|"MODEL_DISABLED"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineModelConfigsValueEnumMap { [string]: gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineModelConfigsValueEnum|string }

---Configurations for a Search Engine.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfig
---@field searchTier? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfigSearchTierEnum|string The search feature tier of this engine. Different tiers might have different pricing. To learn more, check the pricing documentation. Defaults to SearchTier.SEARCH_TIER_STANDARD if not specified.
---@field searchAddOns? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfigSearchAddOnsItemEnumList The add-on that this search engine enables.
---@field requiredSubscriptionTier? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfigRequiredSubscriptionTierEnum|string Optional. The required subscription tier of this engine. If the required subscription tier is search, user with higher license tier like assist can still access the standalone app associated with this engine. Web grounding feature is only available on the app if it is set as SubscriptionTier.SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_SEARCH_AND_ASSISTANT.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfigRequiredSubscriptionTierEnum "SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_UNSPECIFIED"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_SEARCH"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_SEARCH_AND_ASSISTANT"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_NOTEBOOK_LM"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_FRONTLINE_WORKER"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_AGENTSPACE_STARTER"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_AGENTSPACE_BUSINESS"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_ENTERPRISE"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_ENTERPRISE_EMERGING"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_EDU"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_EDU_PRO"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_EDU_EMERGING"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_EDU_PRO_EMERGING"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_FRONTLINE_STARTER"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_CONSUMPTION_ONLY"|"SUBSCRIPTION_TIER_EDU_GOV_EMERGING"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfigSearchAddOnsItemEnum "SEARCH_ADD_ON_UNSPECIFIED"|"SEARCH_ADD_ON_LLM"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfigSearchAddOnsItemEnumList (gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfigSearchAddOnsItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfigSearchTierEnum "SEARCH_TIER_UNSPECIFIED"|"SEARCH_TIER_STANDARD"|"SEARCH_TIER_ENTERPRISE"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSolutionTypeEnum "SOLUTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_GENERATIVE_CHAT"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_AI_MODE"

---Fact Chunk.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FactChunk
---@field sourceMetadata? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringMap More fine-grained information for the source reference.
---@field uri? string The URI of the source.
---@field index? number The index of this chunk. Currently, only used for the streaming mode.
---@field domain? string The domain of the source.
---@field chunkText? string Text content of the fact chunk. Can be at most 10K characters long.
---@field source? string Source from which this fact chunk was retrieved. If it was retrieved from the GroundingFacts provided in the request then this field will contain the index of the specific fact from which this chunk was retrieved.
---@field title? string The title of the source.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FactChunkList gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FactChunk[]

---Information about the user feedback. This information will be used for logging and metrics purpose.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Feedback
---@field dataTermsAccepted? boolean Optional. Whether the customer accepted data use terms.
---@field llmModelVersion? string The version of the LLM model that was used to generate the response.
---@field feedbackType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FeedbackFeedbackTypeEnum|string Required. Indicates whether the user gives a positive or negative feedback.
---@field reasons? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FeedbackReasonsItemEnumList Optional. The reasons why the user gives feedback.
---@field componentVersion? string Optional. The version of the component that this report is being sent from.
---@field modelArmorDisputeInfo? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FeedbackModelArmorDisputeInfo Optional. Optional Model Armor false-positive dispute metadata attached to feedback.
---@field feedbackSource? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FeedbackFeedbackSourceEnum|string Optional. The UI component the user feedback comes from, which could be GOOGLE_CONSOLE, GOOGLE_WIDGET, GOOGLE_WEBAPP.
---@field conversationInfo? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FeedbackConversationInfo The related conversation information when user gives feedback.
---@field comment? string Optional. The additional user comment of the feedback.

---The conversation information such as the question index and session name.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FeedbackConversationInfo
---@field taskName? string Optional. The full resource name of the Sobi task if the conversation was handled by a long-running agent task. Format (canonical, or the short alias the Task API also accepts): projects/{project}/locations/{location}/agents/{agent}/tasks/{task} projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tasks/{task}
---@field assistToken? string Optional. The token which could be used to fetch the assistant log.
---@field stepSeqNum? string Optional. The `TaskServerEvent.seq_num` of the step that opened the rated agent task reply.
---@field questionIndex? number The index of the user input within the conversation messages.
---@field query? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Query Required. The user's search query.
---@field answerQueryToken? string Optional. The token which could be used to fetch the answer log.
---@field trajectoryId? string Optional. The runtime trajectory id of the rated agent task turn, as set on `TaskServerEvent.trajectory_id`. Shared by all steps of the turn.
---@field session? string Name of the newly generated or continued session.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FeedbackFeedbackSourceEnum "FEEDBACK_SOURCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"GOOGLE_CONSOLE"|"GOOGLE_WIDGET"|"GOOGLE_WEBAPP"|"GOOGLE_AGENTSPACE_MOBILE"|"GOOGLE_AGENTSPACE_DESKTOP"

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FeedbackFeedbackTypeEnum "FEEDBACK_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"LIKE"|"DISLIKE"

---Information submitted when a user disputes a Model Armor `BLOCK` or `FLAG` verdict.
---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FeedbackModelArmorDisputeInfo
---@field templateName? string Optional. Resource name of the Model Armor template that produced the sanitization result, in the format `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/templates/{id}`.
---@field expectedLabel? string Optional. The expected-label reason chip selected by the user (for example, "Everyday question" or "Legitimate work-related query").
---@field sanitizationResultJson? string Optional. The raw Model Armor `SanitizationResult`, serialized as JSON.

---@alias gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1FeedbackReasonsItemEnum "REASON_UNSPECIFIED"|"INACCURATE_RESPONSE"|"NOT_RELEVANT"|"INCOMPREHENSIVE"|"OFFENSIVE_OR_UNSAFE"|"FORMAT_AND_STYLES"|"BAD_CITATION"|"CANVAS_NOT_GENERATED"|"CANVAS_QUALITY_BAD"|"CANVAS_EXPORT_FAILED"|"RELEVANT"|"COMPREHENSIVE"|"GOOD_CITATION"|"ACCURATE"

