---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Session to update. The following are NOT supported: * Session.name If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/sessions/*`

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresSiteSearchEngineTargetSitesRequest
---@field siteVerificationInfo? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SiteVerificationInfo Output only. Site ownership and validity verification status.
---@field exactMatch? boolean Immutable. If set to false, a uri_pattern is generated to include all pages whose address contains the provided_uri_pattern. If set to true, an uri_pattern is generated to try to be an exact match of the provided_uri_pattern or just the specific page if the provided_uri_pattern is a specific one. provided_uri_pattern is always normalized to generate the URI pattern to be used by the search engine.
---@field rootDomainUri? string Output only. Root domain of the provided_uri_pattern.
---@field failureReason? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1TargetSiteFailureReason Output only. Failure reason.
---@field generatedUriPattern? string Output only. This is system-generated based on the provided_uri_pattern.
---@field type? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1TargetSiteTypeEnum|string The type of the target site, e.g., whether the site is to be included or excluded.
---@field providedUriPattern? string Required. Input only. The user provided URI pattern from which the `generated_uri_pattern` is generated.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The target site's last updated time.
---@field indexingStatus? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1TargetSiteIndexingStatusEnum|string Output only. Indexing status.
---@field name string Output only. The fully qualified resource name of the target site. `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/siteSearchEngine/targetSites/{target_site}` The `target_site_id` is system-generated.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresWidgetConfigsRequest
---@field enableSearchAsYouType? boolean Whether to enable search-as-you-type behavior for the search widget
---@field nodes? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigNodeList Output only. The nodes associated with the Widget Config.
---@field enableSummarization? boolean Turn on or off summarization for the search response.
---@field fieldsUiComponentsMap? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigUIComponentFieldMap The key is the UI component. Mock. Currently supported `title`, `thumbnail`, `url`, `custom1`, `custom2`, `custom3`. The value is the name of the field along with its device visibility. The 3 custom fields are optional and can be added or removed. `title`, `thumbnail`, `url` are required UI components that cannot be removed.
---@field defaultSearchRequestOrderBy? string The default ordering for search results if specified. Used to set SearchRequest#order_by on applicable requests. https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/docs/reference/rest/v1alpha/projects.locations.dataStores.servingConfigs/search#request-body
---@field customerProvidedConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigCustomerProvidedConfig Optional. Output only. Describes the customer related configurations, currently only used for government customers. This field cannot be modified after project onboarding.
---@field geminiBundle? boolean Output only. Whether the subscription is gemini bundle or not.
---@field dataStoreType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigDataStoreTypeEnum|string Output only. The type of the parent data store.
---@field enableResultScore? boolean Whether to show the result score.
---@field uiSettings? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigUiSettings Describes general widget search settings as seen in cloud console widget configuration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field facetField? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigFacetFieldList The configuration and appearance of facets in the end user view.
---@field dataStoreUiConfigs? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigDataStoreUiConfigList Configurable UI configurations per data store.
---@field assistantSettings? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigAssistantSettings Optional. Output only. Describes the assistant settings of the widget.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was updated.
---@field batchAuthStatuses? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigBatchAuthStatusList Output only. The batch authorization statuses for the widget's connectors.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was created.
---@field configId? string Output only. Unique obfuscated identifier of a WidgetConfig.
---@field uiBranding? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigUiBrandingSettings Describes search widget UI branding settings, such as the widget title, logo, favicons, and colors.
---@field resultDisplayType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigResultDisplayTypeEnum|string The type of snippet to display in UCS widget. - RESULT_DISPLAY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED for existing users. - SNIPPET for new non-enterprise search users. - EXTRACTIVE_ANSWER for new enterprise search users.
---@field collectionComponents? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigCollectionComponentList Output only. Collection components that lists all collections and child data stores associated with the widget config, those data sources can be used for filtering in widget service APIs, users can return results that from selected data sources. For SaaS / Business engines, when `LookupWidgetConfig` is called with `view = WITH_AVAILABLE_CONNECTORS`, this list is additionally augmented with synthetic placeholder entries for connectors the caller may attach but has not yet attached (see `CollectionComponent` for the placeholder contract). The frontend can therefore render a unified list of already-attached and available-to-attach sources by iterating this single field. For Enterprise engines and for the default `view`, only already-attached connectors are returned (today's behavior).
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable widget config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field homepageSetting? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigHomepageSetting Optional. Describes the homepage settings of the widget.
---@field enableSnippetResultSummary? boolean Turn on or off summary for each snippets result.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigIndustryVerticalEnum|string Output only. The industry vertical that the WidgetConfig registers. The WidgetConfig industry vertical is based on the associated Engine.
---@field allowlistedDomains? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Allowlisted domains that can load this widget.
---@field enablePrivateKnowledgeGraph? boolean Optional. Output only. Whether to enable private knowledge graph.
---@field allowPublicAccess? boolean Whether allow no-auth integration with widget. If set true, public access to search or other solutions from widget is allowed without authenication token provided by customer hosted backend server.
---@field accessSettings? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigAccessSettings Will be used for all widget access settings seen in cloud console integration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field enableSafeSearch? boolean Whether to enable safe search.
---@field llmEnabled? boolean Output only. Whether LLM is enabled in the corresponding data store.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that this WidgetConfig can be used for.
---@field enableQualityFeedback? boolean Turn on or off collecting the search result quality feedback from end users.
---@field minimumDataTermAccepted? boolean Output only. Whether the customer accepted data use terms.
---@field enableConversationalSearch? boolean Whether to allow conversational search (LLM, multi-turn) or not (non-LLM, single-turn).
---@field contentSearchSpec? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SearchRequestContentSearchSpec The content search spec that configs the desired behavior of content search.
---@field enableWebApp? boolean Whether to enable standalone web app.
---@field enableAutocomplete? boolean Whether or not to enable autocomplete.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided WidgetConfig to update. The following are the only supported fields: * WidgetConfig.enable_autocomplete If not set, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the widget config. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}/widgetConfigs/{widget_config_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesAssistantsRequest
---@field customerPolicy? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantCustomerPolicy Optional. Customer policy for the assistant.
---@field displayName? string Required. The assistant display name. It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters.
---@field enabledTools? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantToolListMap Optional. The enabled tools on this assistant. The keys are data connector resource names, in the format `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataConnector`. The values are the tools that the admin enabled on that connector. Admins can selectively enable tools on any of the connectors that they created in the project. For example: ``` { "projects/my-project/locations/global/collections/jira1/dataConnector": { "toolInfo": [ { "toolName": "create_jira_issue", "toolDisplayName": "Create Jira issue" }, { "toolName": "update_jira_issue", "toolDisplayName": "Update Jira issue" } ] } } ```
---@field webGroundingType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantWebGroundingTypeEnum|string Optional. The type of web grounding to use.
---@field defaultWebGroundingToggleOff? boolean Optional. This field controls the default web grounding toggle for end users if `web_grounding_type` is set to `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_GOOGLE_SEARCH` or `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_ENTERPRISE_WEB_SEARCH`. By default, this field is set to false. If `web_grounding_type` is `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_GOOGLE_SEARCH` or `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_ENTERPRISE_WEB_SEARCH`, end users will have web grounding enabled by default on UI. If true, grounding toggle will be disabled by default on UI. End users can still enable web grounding in the UI if web grounding is enabled.
---@field description? string Optional. Description for additional information. Expected to be shown on the configuration UI, not to the users of the assistant.
---@field generationConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AssistantGenerationConfig Optional. Configuration for the generation of the assistant response.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Represents the time when this Assistant was most recently updated.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Represents the time when this Assistant was created.
---@field name string Immutable. Resource name of the assistant. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/assistants/{assistant}` It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field updateMask? string The list of fields to update.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesControlsRequest
---@field redirectAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlRedirectAction Defines a redirect-type control.
---@field associatedServingConfigIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Output only. List of all ServingConfig IDs this control is attached to. May take up to 10 minutes to update after changes.
---@field conditions? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionList Determines when the associated action will trigger. Omit to always apply the action. Currently only a single condition may be specified. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field useCases? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlUseCasesItemEnumList Specifies the use case for the control. Affects what condition fields can be set. Only applies to SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH. Currently only allow one use case per control. Must be set when solution_type is SolutionType.SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. What solution the control belongs to. Must be compatible with vertical of resource. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field displayName? string Required. Human readable name. The identifier used in UI views. Must be UTF-8 encoded string. Length limit is 128 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field boostAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostAction Defines a boost-type control
---@field synonymsAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlSynonymsAction Treats a group of terms as synonyms of one another.
---@field filterAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlFilterAction Defines a filter-type control Currently not supported by Recommendation
---@field promoteAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlPromoteAction Promote certain links based on predefined trigger queries.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/*/locations/global/dataStore/*/controls/*`
---@field updateMask? string Optional. Indicates which fields in the provided Control to update. The following are NOT supported: * Control.name * Control.solution_type If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesConversationsRequest
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the conversation started.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the conversation finished.
---@field messages? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationMessageList Conversation messages.
---@field state? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationStateEnum|string The state of the Conversation.
---@field userPseudoId? string A unique identifier for tracking users.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/dataStore/*/conversations/*` or `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/*/conversations/*`.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Conversation to update. The following are NOT supported: * Conversation.name If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesRequest
---@field cmekConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CmekConfig Output only. CMEK-related information for the Engine.
---@field chatEngineMetadata? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineChatEngineMetadata Output only. Additional information of the Chat Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineIndustryVerticalEnum|string Optional. The industry vertical that the engine registers. The restriction of the Engine industry vertical is based on DataStore: Vertical on Engine has to match vertical of the DataStore linked to the engine.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Recommendation Engine was last updated.
---@field searchEngineConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSearchEngineConfig Configurations for the Search Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Recommendation Engine was created at.
---@field sessionConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SessionConfig Optional. Non-empty default. Session config for the engine.
---@field connectorTenantInfo? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringMap Optional. Maps a connector ID (e.g., "hybrid-github", "shopify") to tenant-specific information required for that connector. The structure of the tenant information string is connector-dependent.
---@field modelConfigs? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineModelConfigsValueEnumMap Optional. Maps a model name to its specific configuration for this engine. This allows admin users to turn on/off individual models. This only stores models whose states are overridden by the admin. When the state is unspecified, or model_configs is empty for this model, the system will decide if this model should be available or not based on the default configuration. For example, a preview model should be disabled by default if the admin has not chosen to enable it.
---@field effectiveFeatures? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineEffectiveFeaturesValueEnumMap Output only. The complete, server-resolved state of every known feature toggle. Unlike `features`, which stores only explicit admin overrides, this map always contains an entry for every toggle. Clients should read toggle state from this field.
---@field associatedAgentRegistry? string Output only. The Agent registry containing the agents, MCP servers and tools associated with this engine. Derived server-side from the linked Agent Gateway's registry.
---@field observabilityConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ObservabilityConfig Optional. Observability config for the engine.
---@field chatEngineConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineChatEngineConfig Configurations for the Chat Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT.
---@field features? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturesValueEnumMap Optional. Feature config for the engine to opt in or opt out of features. Supported keys: * `*`: all features, if it's present, all other feature state settings are ignored. * `agent-gallery` * `no-code-agent-builder` * `prompt-gallery` * `model-selector` * `notebook-lm` * `people-search` * `people-search-org-chart` * `bi-directional-audio` * `speech-to-text` * `feedback` * `session-sharing` * `personalization-memory` * `personalization-suggested-highlights` * `mobile-app-access` * `disable-agent-sharing` * `disable-image-generation` * `disable-video-generation` * `music-generation` * `speech-generation` * `disable-onedrive-upload` * `disable-talk-to-content` * `disable-google-drive-upload` * `disable-welcome-emails` * `disable-canvas` * `canvas-workspace` * `canvas-app-builder` * `skills` * `skill-sharing` * `skill-sharing-without-admin-approval` * `skill-security-scan` * `disable-projects` * `sobi` * `enable-end-user-sharing-with-groups` * `single-agent-orchestration` * `multi-agent-orchestration` * `cross-product-intelligence` * `workflow-agents` * `in-app-notifications` * `code-extraction` * `remote-vm` * `license-tier-badge` * `canvas-app-sharing` * `agent-marketplace` * `agent-scheduling` * `preview-agents` * `plugins`
---@field globalFeatureToggleState? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineGlobalFeatureToggleStateEnum|string Optional. Controls the global feature toggle state for the engine.
---@field delayedGlobalFeatureToggleStateAllowed? boolean Output only. Whether the project is allowed to set `global_feature_toggle_state` to `DELAYED`.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the engine. Should be human readable. UTF-8 encoded string with limit of 1024 characters.
---@field procurementContactEmails? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. The emails of the procurement contacts.
---@field dataStoreIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. The data stores associated with this engine. For SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH and SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION type of engines, they can only associate with at most one data store. If solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT, multiple DataStores in the same Collection can be associated here. Note that when used in CreateEngineRequest, one DataStore id must be provided as the system will use it for necessary initializations.
---@field marketplaceAgentVisibility? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMarketplaceAgentVisibilityEnum|string Optional. The visibility of marketplace agents in the agent gallery.
---@field featurePolicies? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineFeaturePolicyMap Optional. Per-feature access policies, keyed by feature toggle name (see `features`). A feature with no entry is available to every user when it is on. Only features that support access policies are accepted.
---@field mediaRecommendationEngineConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfig Configurations for the Media Engine. Only applicable on the data stores with solution_type SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION and IndustryVertical.MEDIA vertical.
---@field knowledgeGraphConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineKnowledgeGraphConfig Optional. Configurations for the Knowledge Graph. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field agentGatewaySetting? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AgentGatewaySetting Optional. The agent gateway setting for the engine.
---@field commonConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineCommonConfig Common config spec that specifies the metadata of the engine.
---@field disableAnalytics? boolean Optional. Whether to disable analytics for searches performed on this engine.
---@field appType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineAppTypeEnum|string Optional. Immutable. This the application type which this engine resource represents. NOTE: this is a new concept independ of existing industry vertical or solution type.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. The solutions of the engine.
---@field configurableBillingApproach? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1EngineConfigurableBillingApproachEnum|string Optional. Configuration for configurable billing approach.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Engine to update. If an unsupported or unknown field is provided, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field name string Immutable. Identifier. The fully qualified resource name of the engine. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}` engine should be 1-63 characters, and valid characters are /a-z0-9*/. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesServingConfigsRequest
---@field synonymsControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition synonyms specifications. If multiple synonyms conditions match, all matching synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field diversityLevel? string How much diversity to use in recommendation model results e.g. `medium-diversity` or `high-diversity`. Currently supported values: * `no-diversity` * `low-diversity` * `medium-diversity` * `high-diversity` * `auto-diversity` If not specified, we choose default based on recommendation model type. Default value: `no-diversity`. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field promoteControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition promote specifications. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable serving config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field createTime? string Output only. ServingConfig created timestamp.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. ServingConfig updated timestamp.
---@field boostControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Boost controls to use in serving path. All triggered boost controls will be applied. Boost controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 boost controls.
---@field rankingExpression? string The ranking expression controls the customized ranking on retrieval documents. To leverage this, document embedding is required. The ranking expression setting in ServingConfig applies to all search requests served by the serving config. However, if `SearchRequest.ranking_expression` is specified, it overrides the ServingConfig ranking expression. The ranking expression is a single function or multiple functions that are joined by "+". * ranking_expression = function, { " + ", function }; Supported functions: * double * relevance_score * double * dotProduct(embedding_field_path) Function variables: * `relevance_score`: pre-defined keywords, used for measure relevance between query and document. * `embedding_field_path`: the document embedding field used with query embedding vector. * `dotProduct`: embedding function between embedding_field_path and query embedding vector. Example ranking expression: If document has an embedding field doc_embedding, the ranking expression could be `0.5 * relevance_score + 0.3 * dotProduct(doc_embedding)`.
---@field dissociateControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition do not associate specifications. If multiple do not associate conditions match, all matching do not associate controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field redirectControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList IDs of the redirect controls. Only the first triggered redirect action is applied, even if multiple apply. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field replacementControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition replacement specifications. Applied according to the order in the list. A previously replaced term can not be re-replaced. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field mediaConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ServingConfigMediaConfig The MediaConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field filterControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Filter controls to use in serving path. All triggered filter controls will be applied. Filter controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 filter controls.
---@field modelId? string The id of the model to use at serving time. Currently only RecommendationModels are supported. Can be changed but only to a compatible model (e.g. others-you-may-like CTR to others-you-may-like CVR). Required when SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field onewaySynonymsControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition oneway synonyms specifications. If multiple oneway synonyms conditions match, all matching oneway synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field ignoreControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition ignore specifications. If multiple ignore conditions match, all matching ignore controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field answerGenerationSpec? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AnswerGenerationSpec Optional. The specification for answer generation.
---@field genericConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ServingConfigGenericConfig The GenericConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ServingConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that a serving config can be associated with.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/engines/{engine_id}/servingConfigs/{serving_config_id}`
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided ServingConfig to update. The following are NOT supported: * ServingConfig.name If not set, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesSessionsRequest
---@field turns? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SessionTurnList Turns.
---@field labels? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. The labels for the session. Can be set as filter in ListSessionsRequest.
---@field pendingAsyncAssistOperationId? string Output only. Full resource name of an in-progress AsyncAssist operation for this session, e.g. `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/engines/*/sessions/*/operations/*`. Set when the operation starts and cleared when it finishes.
---@field isPinned? boolean Optional. Whether the session is pinned, pinned session will be displayed on the top of the session list.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the session finished.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of the session. This field is used to identify the session in the UI. By default, the display name is the first turn query text in the session.
---@field userPseudoId? string A unique identifier for tracking users.
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the session started.
---@field state? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SessionStateEnum|string The state of the session.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Session to update. The following are NOT supported: * Session.name If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/sessions/*`

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesWidgetConfigsRequest
---@field enableSearchAsYouType? boolean Whether to enable search-as-you-type behavior for the search widget
---@field nodes? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigNodeList Output only. The nodes associated with the Widget Config.
---@field enableSummarization? boolean Turn on or off summarization for the search response.
---@field fieldsUiComponentsMap? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigUIComponentFieldMap The key is the UI component. Mock. Currently supported `title`, `thumbnail`, `url`, `custom1`, `custom2`, `custom3`. The value is the name of the field along with its device visibility. The 3 custom fields are optional and can be added or removed. `title`, `thumbnail`, `url` are required UI components that cannot be removed.
---@field defaultSearchRequestOrderBy? string The default ordering for search results if specified. Used to set SearchRequest#order_by on applicable requests. https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/docs/reference/rest/v1alpha/projects.locations.dataStores.servingConfigs/search#request-body
---@field customerProvidedConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigCustomerProvidedConfig Optional. Output only. Describes the customer related configurations, currently only used for government customers. This field cannot be modified after project onboarding.
---@field geminiBundle? boolean Output only. Whether the subscription is gemini bundle or not.
---@field dataStoreType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigDataStoreTypeEnum|string Output only. The type of the parent data store.
---@field enableResultScore? boolean Whether to show the result score.
---@field uiSettings? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigUiSettings Describes general widget search settings as seen in cloud console widget configuration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field facetField? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigFacetFieldList The configuration and appearance of facets in the end user view.
---@field dataStoreUiConfigs? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigDataStoreUiConfigList Configurable UI configurations per data store.
---@field assistantSettings? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigAssistantSettings Optional. Output only. Describes the assistant settings of the widget.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was updated.
---@field batchAuthStatuses? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigBatchAuthStatusList Output only. The batch authorization statuses for the widget's connectors.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was created.
---@field configId? string Output only. Unique obfuscated identifier of a WidgetConfig.
---@field uiBranding? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigUiBrandingSettings Describes search widget UI branding settings, such as the widget title, logo, favicons, and colors.
---@field resultDisplayType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigResultDisplayTypeEnum|string The type of snippet to display in UCS widget. - RESULT_DISPLAY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED for existing users. - SNIPPET for new non-enterprise search users. - EXTRACTIVE_ANSWER for new enterprise search users.
---@field collectionComponents? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigCollectionComponentList Output only. Collection components that lists all collections and child data stores associated with the widget config, those data sources can be used for filtering in widget service APIs, users can return results that from selected data sources. For SaaS / Business engines, when `LookupWidgetConfig` is called with `view = WITH_AVAILABLE_CONNECTORS`, this list is additionally augmented with synthetic placeholder entries for connectors the caller may attach but has not yet attached (see `CollectionComponent` for the placeholder contract). The frontend can therefore render a unified list of already-attached and available-to-attach sources by iterating this single field. For Enterprise engines and for the default `view`, only already-attached connectors are returned (today's behavior).
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable widget config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field homepageSetting? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigHomepageSetting Optional. Describes the homepage settings of the widget.
---@field enableSnippetResultSummary? boolean Turn on or off summary for each snippets result.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigIndustryVerticalEnum|string Output only. The industry vertical that the WidgetConfig registers. The WidgetConfig industry vertical is based on the associated Engine.
---@field allowlistedDomains? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Allowlisted domains that can load this widget.
---@field enablePrivateKnowledgeGraph? boolean Optional. Output only. Whether to enable private knowledge graph.
---@field allowPublicAccess? boolean Whether allow no-auth integration with widget. If set true, public access to search or other solutions from widget is allowed without authenication token provided by customer hosted backend server.
---@field accessSettings? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigAccessSettings Will be used for all widget access settings seen in cloud console integration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field enableSafeSearch? boolean Whether to enable safe search.
---@field llmEnabled? boolean Output only. Whether LLM is enabled in the corresponding data store.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that this WidgetConfig can be used for.
---@field enableQualityFeedback? boolean Turn on or off collecting the search result quality feedback from end users.
---@field minimumDataTermAccepted? boolean Output only. Whether the customer accepted data use terms.
---@field enableConversationalSearch? boolean Whether to allow conversational search (LLM, multi-turn) or not (non-LLM, single-turn).
---@field contentSearchSpec? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SearchRequestContentSearchSpec The content search spec that configs the desired behavior of content search.
---@field enableWebApp? boolean Whether to enable standalone web app.
---@field enableAutocomplete? boolean Whether or not to enable autocomplete.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the widget config. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}/widgetConfigs/{widget_config_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided WidgetConfig to update. The following are the only supported fields: * WidgetConfig.enable_autocomplete If not set, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresBranchesDocumentsRequest
---@field parentDocumentId? string The identifier of the parent document. Currently supports at most two level document hierarchy. Id should conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) standard with a length limit of 63 characters.
---@field derivedStructData? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.DocumentMap Output only. This field is OUTPUT_ONLY. It contains derived data that are not in the original input document.
---@field indexStatus? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentIndexStatus Output only. The index status of the document. * If document is indexed successfully, the index_time field is populated. * Otherwise, if document is not indexed due to errors, the error_samples field is populated. * Otherwise, if document's index is in progress, the pending_message field is populated.
---@field id? string Immutable. The identifier of the document. Id should conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) standard with a length limit of 128 characters.
---@field structData? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.DocumentMap The structured JSON data for the document. It should conform to the registered Schema or an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is thrown.
---@field jsonData? string The JSON string representation of the document. It should conform to the registered Schema or an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is thrown.
---@field content? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentContent The unstructured data linked to this document. Content can only be set and must be set if this document is under a `CONTENT_REQUIRED` data store.
---@field indexTime? string Output only. The time when the document was last indexed. If this field is populated, it means the document has been indexed. While documents typically become searchable within seconds of indexing, it can sometimes take up to a few hours. If this field is not populated, it means the document has never been indexed.
---@field schemaId? string The identifier of the schema located in the same data store.
---@field aclInfo? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentAclInfo Access control information for the document.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the document. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/branches/{branch}/documents/{document_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field allowMissing? boolean If set to `true` and the Document is not found, a new Document is be created.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided imported 'document' to update. If not set, by default updates all fields.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresControlsRequest
---@field redirectAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlRedirectAction Defines a redirect-type control.
---@field associatedServingConfigIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Output only. List of all ServingConfig IDs this control is attached to. May take up to 10 minutes to update after changes.
---@field conditions? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConditionList Determines when the associated action will trigger. Omit to always apply the action. Currently only a single condition may be specified. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field useCases? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlUseCasesItemEnumList Specifies the use case for the control. Affects what condition fields can be set. Only applies to SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH. Currently only allow one use case per control. Must be set when solution_type is SolutionType.SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. What solution the control belongs to. Must be compatible with vertical of resource. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field displayName? string Required. Human readable name. The identifier used in UI views. Must be UTF-8 encoded string. Length limit is 128 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field boostAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlBoostAction Defines a boost-type control
---@field synonymsAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlSynonymsAction Treats a group of terms as synonyms of one another.
---@field filterAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlFilterAction Defines a filter-type control Currently not supported by Recommendation
---@field promoteAction? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ControlPromoteAction Promote certain links based on predefined trigger queries.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. Indicates which fields in the provided Control to update. The following are NOT supported: * Control.name * Control.solution_type If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/*/locations/global/dataStore/*/controls/*`

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresConversationsRequest
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the conversation started.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the conversation finished.
---@field messages? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationMessageList Conversation messages.
---@field state? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ConversationStateEnum|string The state of the Conversation.
---@field userPseudoId? string A unique identifier for tracking users.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Conversation to update. The following are NOT supported: * Conversation.name If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/dataStore/*/conversations/*` or `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/*/conversations/*`.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresRequest
---@field configurableBillingApproachUpdateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when configurable_billing_approach was last updated.
---@field aclEnabled? boolean Immutable. Whether data in the DataStore has ACL information. If set to `true`, the source data must have ACL. ACL will be ingested when data is ingested by DocumentService.ImportDocuments methods. When ACL is enabled for the DataStore, Document can't be accessed by calling DocumentService.GetDocument or DocumentService.ListDocuments. Currently ACL is only supported in `GENERIC` industry vertical with non-`PUBLIC_WEBSITE` content config.
---@field kmsKeyName? string Input only. The KMS key to be used to protect this DataStore at creation time. Must be set for requests that need to comply with CMEK Org Policy protections. If this field is set and processed successfully, the DataStore will be protected by the KMS key, as indicated in the cmek_config field.
---@field defaultSchemaId? string Output only. The id of the default Schema associated to this data store.
---@field contentConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataStoreContentConfigEnum|string Immutable. The content config of the data store. If this field is unset, the server behavior defaults to ContentConfig.NO_CONTENT.
---@field configurableBillingApproach? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataStoreConfigurableBillingApproachEnum|string Optional. Configuration for configurable billing approach. See
---@field isInfobotFaqDataStore? boolean Optional. If set, this DataStore is an Infobot FAQ DataStore.
---@field naturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1NaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingConfig Optional. Configuration for Natural Language Query Understanding.
---@field dataProtectionPolicy? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataProtectionPolicy Optional. Specifies the data protection policy for the data store.
---@field advancedSiteSearchConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AdvancedSiteSearchConfig Optional. Configuration for advanced site search.
---@field cmekConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1CmekConfig Output only. CMEK-related information for the DataStore.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the DataStore was created at.
---@field solutionTypes? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataStoreSolutionTypesItemEnumList The solutions that the data store enrolls. Available solutions for each industry_vertical: * `MEDIA`: `SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION` and `SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH`. * `SITE_SEARCH`: `SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH` is automatically enrolled. Other solutions cannot be enrolled.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataStoreIndustryVerticalEnum|string Immutable. The industry vertical that the data store registers.
---@field startingSchema? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1Schema The start schema to use for this DataStore when provisioning it. If unset, a default vertical specialized schema will be used. This field is only used by CreateDataStore API, and will be ignored if used in other APIs. This field will be omitted from all API responses including CreateDataStore API. To retrieve a schema of a DataStore, use SchemaService.GetSchema API instead. The provided schema will be validated against certain rules on schema. Learn more from [this doc](https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/docs/provide-schema).
---@field displayName? string Required. The data store display name. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field identityMappingStore? string Immutable. The fully qualified resource name of the associated IdentityMappingStore. This field can only be set for acl_enabled DataStores with `THIRD_PARTY` or `GSUITE` IdP. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/identityMappingStores/{identity_mapping_store}`.
---@field billingEstimation? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataStoreBillingEstimation Output only. Data size estimation for billing.
---@field federatedSearchConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataStoreFederatedSearchConfig Optional. If set, this DataStore is a federated search DataStore.
---@field healthcareFhirConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1HealthcareFhirConfig Optional. Configuration for `HEALTHCARE_FHIR` vertical.
---@field servingConfigDataStore? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DataStoreServingConfigDataStore Optional. Stores serving config at DataStore level.
---@field workspaceConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WorkspaceConfig Config to store data store type configuration for workspace data. This must be set when DataStore.content_config is set as DataStore.ContentConfig.GOOGLE_WORKSPACE.
---@field documentProcessingConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1DocumentProcessingConfig Configuration for Document understanding and enrichment.
---@field name string Immutable. Identifier. The full resource name of the data store. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided DataStore to update. If an unsupported or unknown field is provided, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresSchemasRequest
---@field jsonSchema? string The JSON representation of the schema.
---@field structSchema? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.DocumentMap The structured representation of the schema.
---@field allowMissing? boolean If set to true, and the Schema is not found, a new Schema is created. In this situation, `update_mask` is ignored.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the schema, in the format of `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/schemas/{schema}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresServingConfigsRequest
---@field synonymsControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition synonyms specifications. If multiple synonyms conditions match, all matching synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field diversityLevel? string How much diversity to use in recommendation model results e.g. `medium-diversity` or `high-diversity`. Currently supported values: * `no-diversity` * `low-diversity` * `medium-diversity` * `high-diversity` * `auto-diversity` If not specified, we choose default based on recommendation model type. Default value: `no-diversity`. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field promoteControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition promote specifications. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable serving config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field createTime? string Output only. ServingConfig created timestamp.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. ServingConfig updated timestamp.
---@field boostControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Boost controls to use in serving path. All triggered boost controls will be applied. Boost controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 boost controls.
---@field rankingExpression? string The ranking expression controls the customized ranking on retrieval documents. To leverage this, document embedding is required. The ranking expression setting in ServingConfig applies to all search requests served by the serving config. However, if `SearchRequest.ranking_expression` is specified, it overrides the ServingConfig ranking expression. The ranking expression is a single function or multiple functions that are joined by "+". * ranking_expression = function, { " + ", function }; Supported functions: * double * relevance_score * double * dotProduct(embedding_field_path) Function variables: * `relevance_score`: pre-defined keywords, used for measure relevance between query and document. * `embedding_field_path`: the document embedding field used with query embedding vector. * `dotProduct`: embedding function between embedding_field_path and query embedding vector. Example ranking expression: If document has an embedding field doc_embedding, the ranking expression could be `0.5 * relevance_score + 0.3 * dotProduct(doc_embedding)`.
---@field dissociateControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition do not associate specifications. If multiple do not associate conditions match, all matching do not associate controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field redirectControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList IDs of the redirect controls. Only the first triggered redirect action is applied, even if multiple apply. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field replacementControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition replacement specifications. Applied according to the order in the list. A previously replaced term can not be re-replaced. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field mediaConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ServingConfigMediaConfig The MediaConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field filterControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Filter controls to use in serving path. All triggered filter controls will be applied. Filter controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 filter controls.
---@field modelId? string The id of the model to use at serving time. Currently only RecommendationModels are supported. Can be changed but only to a compatible model (e.g. others-you-may-like CTR to others-you-may-like CVR). Required when SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field onewaySynonymsControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition oneway synonyms specifications. If multiple oneway synonyms conditions match, all matching oneway synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field ignoreControlIds? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Condition ignore specifications. If multiple ignore conditions match, all matching ignore controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field answerGenerationSpec? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1AnswerGenerationSpec Optional. The specification for answer generation.
---@field genericConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ServingConfigGenericConfig The GenericConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ServingConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that a serving config can be associated with.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/engines/{engine_id}/servingConfigs/{serving_config_id}`
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided ServingConfig to update. The following are NOT supported: * ServingConfig.name If not set, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresSessionsRequest
---@field turns? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SessionTurnList Turns.
---@field labels? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Optional. The labels for the session. Can be set as filter in ListSessionsRequest.
---@field pendingAsyncAssistOperationId? string Output only. Full resource name of an in-progress AsyncAssist operation for this session, e.g. `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/engines/*/sessions/*/operations/*`. Set when the operation starts and cleared when it finishes.
---@field isPinned? boolean Optional. Whether the session is pinned, pinned session will be displayed on the top of the session list.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the session finished.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of the session. This field is used to identify the session in the UI. By default, the display name is the first turn query text in the session.
---@field userPseudoId? string A unique identifier for tracking users.
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the session started.
---@field state? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SessionStateEnum|string The state of the session.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/sessions/*`
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Session to update. The following are NOT supported: * Session.name If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresSiteSearchEngineTargetSitesRequest
---@field siteVerificationInfo? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SiteVerificationInfo Output only. Site ownership and validity verification status.
---@field exactMatch? boolean Immutable. If set to false, a uri_pattern is generated to include all pages whose address contains the provided_uri_pattern. If set to true, an uri_pattern is generated to try to be an exact match of the provided_uri_pattern or just the specific page if the provided_uri_pattern is a specific one. provided_uri_pattern is always normalized to generate the URI pattern to be used by the search engine.
---@field rootDomainUri? string Output only. Root domain of the provided_uri_pattern.
---@field failureReason? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1TargetSiteFailureReason Output only. Failure reason.
---@field generatedUriPattern? string Output only. This is system-generated based on the provided_uri_pattern.
---@field type? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1TargetSiteTypeEnum|string The type of the target site, e.g., whether the site is to be included or excluded.
---@field providedUriPattern? string Required. Input only. The user provided URI pattern from which the `generated_uri_pattern` is generated.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The target site's last updated time.
---@field indexingStatus? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1TargetSiteIndexingStatusEnum|string Output only. Indexing status.
---@field name string Output only. The fully qualified resource name of the target site. `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/siteSearchEngine/targetSites/{target_site}` The `target_site_id` is system-generated.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresWidgetConfigsRequest
---@field enableSearchAsYouType? boolean Whether to enable search-as-you-type behavior for the search widget
---@field nodes? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigNodeList Output only. The nodes associated with the Widget Config.
---@field enableSummarization? boolean Turn on or off summarization for the search response.
---@field fieldsUiComponentsMap? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigUIComponentFieldMap The key is the UI component. Mock. Currently supported `title`, `thumbnail`, `url`, `custom1`, `custom2`, `custom3`. The value is the name of the field along with its device visibility. The 3 custom fields are optional and can be added or removed. `title`, `thumbnail`, `url` are required UI components that cannot be removed.
---@field defaultSearchRequestOrderBy? string The default ordering for search results if specified. Used to set SearchRequest#order_by on applicable requests. https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/docs/reference/rest/v1alpha/projects.locations.dataStores.servingConfigs/search#request-body
---@field customerProvidedConfig? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigCustomerProvidedConfig Optional. Output only. Describes the customer related configurations, currently only used for government customers. This field cannot be modified after project onboarding.
---@field geminiBundle? boolean Output only. Whether the subscription is gemini bundle or not.
---@field dataStoreType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigDataStoreTypeEnum|string Output only. The type of the parent data store.
---@field enableResultScore? boolean Whether to show the result score.
---@field uiSettings? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigUiSettings Describes general widget search settings as seen in cloud console widget configuration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field facetField? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigFacetFieldList The configuration and appearance of facets in the end user view.
---@field dataStoreUiConfigs? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigDataStoreUiConfigList Configurable UI configurations per data store.
---@field assistantSettings? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigAssistantSettings Optional. Output only. Describes the assistant settings of the widget.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was updated.
---@field batchAuthStatuses? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigBatchAuthStatusList Output only. The batch authorization statuses for the widget's connectors.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was created.
---@field configId? string Output only. Unique obfuscated identifier of a WidgetConfig.
---@field uiBranding? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigUiBrandingSettings Describes search widget UI branding settings, such as the widget title, logo, favicons, and colors.
---@field resultDisplayType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigResultDisplayTypeEnum|string The type of snippet to display in UCS widget. - RESULT_DISPLAY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED for existing users. - SNIPPET for new non-enterprise search users. - EXTRACTIVE_ANSWER for new enterprise search users.
---@field collectionComponents? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigCollectionComponentList Output only. Collection components that lists all collections and child data stores associated with the widget config, those data sources can be used for filtering in widget service APIs, users can return results that from selected data sources. For SaaS / Business engines, when `LookupWidgetConfig` is called with `view = WITH_AVAILABLE_CONNECTORS`, this list is additionally augmented with synthetic placeholder entries for connectors the caller may attach but has not yet attached (see `CollectionComponent` for the placeholder contract). The frontend can therefore render a unified list of already-attached and available-to-attach sources by iterating this single field. For Enterprise engines and for the default `view`, only already-attached connectors are returned (today's behavior).
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable widget config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field homepageSetting? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigHomepageSetting Optional. Describes the homepage settings of the widget.
---@field enableSnippetResultSummary? boolean Turn on or off summary for each snippets result.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigIndustryVerticalEnum|string Output only. The industry vertical that the WidgetConfig registers. The WidgetConfig industry vertical is based on the associated Engine.
---@field allowlistedDomains? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.StringList Allowlisted domains that can load this widget.
---@field enablePrivateKnowledgeGraph? boolean Optional. Output only. Whether to enable private knowledge graph.
---@field allowPublicAccess? boolean Whether allow no-auth integration with widget. If set true, public access to search or other solutions from widget is allowed without authenication token provided by customer hosted backend server.
---@field accessSettings? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigAccessSettings Will be used for all widget access settings seen in cloud console integration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field enableSafeSearch? boolean Whether to enable safe search.
---@field llmEnabled? boolean Output only. Whether LLM is enabled in the corresponding data store.
---@field solutionType? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1WidgetConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that this WidgetConfig can be used for.
---@field enableQualityFeedback? boolean Turn on or off collecting the search result quality feedback from end users.
---@field minimumDataTermAccepted? boolean Output only. Whether the customer accepted data use terms.
---@field enableConversationalSearch? boolean Whether to allow conversational search (LLM, multi-turn) or not (non-LLM, single-turn).
---@field contentSearchSpec? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1SearchRequestContentSearchSpec The content search spec that configs the desired behavior of content search.
---@field enableWebApp? boolean Whether to enable standalone web app.
---@field enableAutocomplete? boolean Whether or not to enable autocomplete.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided WidgetConfig to update. The following are the only supported fields: * WidgetConfig.enable_autocomplete If not set, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the widget config. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}/widgetConfigs/{widget_config_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsLicenseConfigsRequest
---@field endDate? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleTypeDate Optional. The planed end date.
---@field subscriptionTerm? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1LicenseConfigSubscriptionTermEnum|string Required. Subscription term.
---@field earlyTerminationDate? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleTypeDate Output only. The date when the subscription is terminated earlier than the expiration date.
---@field freeTrial? boolean Optional. Whether the license config is for free trial.
---@field startDate? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleTypeDate Required. The start date.
---@field geminiBundle? boolean Output only. Whether the license config is for Gemini bundle.
---@field state? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1LicenseConfigStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the license config.
---@field earlyTerminated? boolean Output only. Indication of whether the subscription is terminated earlier than the expiration date.
---@field autoRenew? boolean Optional. Whether the license config should be auto renewed when it reaches the end date.
---@field lastUserUpdateTime? string Optional. Timestamp of the most recent user-initiated update (seat count change or subscription term change). Unlike `update_time`, this field is only stamped when a customer explicitly updates the license (e.g. via the UI), and is not touched by system-driven writes (subscription pipeline, BALC propagation, etc.).
---@field subscriptionTier? gcp.discoveryengine_v1.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1LicenseConfigSubscriptionTierEnum|string Required. Subscription tier information for the license config.
---@field licenseCount? string Required. Number of licenses purchased.
---@field name string Immutable. Identifier. The fully qualified resource name of the license config. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/licenseConfigs/{license_config}`
---@field updateMask? string Optional. Indicates which fields in the provided LicenseConfig to update. If an unsupported or unknown field is provided, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.

---@class gcp.discoveryengine_v1.PatchProjectsLocationsUserStoresRequest
---@field enableExpiredLicenseAutoUpdate? boolean Optional. Whether to enable license auto update for users in this User Store. If true, users with expired licenses will automatically be updated to use the default license config as long as the default license config has seats left.
---@field defaultLicenseConfig? string Optional. The default subscription LicenseConfig for the UserStore, if UserStore.enable_license_auto_register is true, new users will automatically register under the default subscription. If default LicenseConfig doesn't have remaining license seats left, new users will not be assigned with license and will be blocked for Vertex AI Search features. This is used if `license_assignment_tier_rules` is not configured.
---@field enableLicenseAutoRegister? boolean Optional. Whether to enable license auto register for users in this User Store. If true, new users will automatically register under the default license config as long as the default license config has seats left.
---@field displayName? string The display name of the User Store.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. The list of fields to update.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the User Store, in the format of `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/userStores/{user_store}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.

